msgctxt "help/60/0"
msgid "Welcome!"
msgstr "Bienvenue!"

msgctxt "help/60/1"
msgid ""
"This tutorial will take you through the first steps of building a "
"thriving Roman city.  It will introduce game features one at a time, "
"and give you a chance to try each one out.\n"
"You can pause and unpause the sample game at any time by pressing the "
"\"P\" key.  To exit the sample game and continue with the tutorial, click "
"on the Exit button.\n"
"A mouse is required to play CAESAR II. When you are told to \"click on,\" "
"\"press\" or \"select\" something, use the left mouse button.\n"
"\n"
"-     Press this to see the last page you read.\n"
"\n"
"-     Press this to skip these introductory pages, and start building "
"right away.\n"
"\n"
"-     Press this to see the next page in the tutorial.\n"
"\n"
"-     Press this to exit the tutorial.\n"
"\n"
"Now press the button to move to the next page."
msgstr ""
"Ce tutorial vous explique les premières étapes à franchir pour bâtir "
"une cité Romaine. Il introduit un élément du jeu à la fois et vous "
"permet de les essayer.\n"
"Vous pouvez mettre en pause et reprendre le jeu à tout moment en "
"appuyant sur \"P\". Pour quitter le jeu et continuer le tutorial, cliquez "
"sur Exit.\n"
"Pour jouer à CAESAR II, il vous faut une souris. Lorsqu'on vous demande "
"de \"cliquer\", utilisez le bouton gauche de la souris.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"-     Appuyez ici pour relire la dernière page.\n"
"\n"
"-     Appuyez ici pour passer cette introduction et commencer à "
"construire.\n"
"\n"
"-     Appuyez ici pour lire la page suivante du tutorial.\n"
"\n"
"-     Appuyez ici pour quitter le tutorial.\n"
"\n"
"Pressez une touche pour atteindre la page suivante."

msgctxt "help/61/0"
msgid "The Object of CAESAR"
msgstr "Le but de CAESAR II"

msgctxt "help/61/1"
msgid ""
"YOU are a low-ranking Roman, charged with bringing Peace, Prosperity, "
"Culture and Empire to an untamed world.  The Empire is made up of "
"PROVINCES, which are ruled by Governors.  You are the Governor of one "
"of these provinces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Each province contains a Capital City, which you must build to "
"greatness.  Each province also contains towns and resources that you "
"connect to your city, as well as enemies to defend against.  However, "
"you can choose to play a simplified version of the game, where you only "
"have to worry about what the City needs.  This tutorial uses the basic, "
"CITY-ONLY game."
msgstr ""
"Vous êtes un Citoyen Romain de base, chargé d'amener la Paix, la "
"Prospérité, la culture et l'Empire dans un monde sauvage. L'Empire est "
"constitué de Provinces, administrées par des Gouverneurs. Vous êtes le "
"Gouverneur de l'une d'elles.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
" Chaque Province a une capitale que vous devez mener à la grandeur. "
"Elle possède aussi des villes et des ressources à relier à votre cité "
"et défendre contre les ennemis. Cependant, vous pouvez choisir de ne "
"jouer qu'une version simplifiée du jeu dans laquelle vous ne vous "
"soucierez que de la cité. Ce tutorial utilise la base : le MODE CITE."

msgctxt "help/62/0"
msgid "The City Screen"
msgstr "L'Ecran Cité"

msgctxt "help/62/1"
msgid ""
"You view your Capital through the City Screen (shown here smaller than "
"normal size).  The left part of this screen is the MAIN MAP VIEW, which "
"shows part of the area where you will build your city -- a grassy plain "
"with a river running through it. At the right is the control column, "
"which has two main parts: an OVERVIEW MAP which shows an overhead view "
"of your entire city, and banks of ICONS that let you perform different "
"actions."
msgstr ""
"Cet écran montre votre ville en représentation réduite. La partie "
"gauche de l'écran est la VUE PRINCIPALE, qui montre la zone où vous "
"construirez votre cité -- une plaine herbagée traversée par une "
"rivière. A droite se trouve la colonne de contrôle, avec deux parties "
"principales: une VUE GENERALE montrant l'aspect global de votre cité, "
"et une série d'icônes permettant d'accomplir des actions."

msgctxt "help/63/0"
msgid "Changing the View"
msgstr "Changer de vue"

msgctxt "help/63/1"
msgid ""
"You can do several things to change your view of the city.\n"
"\n"
"If you point to any part of the Overview Map with your mouse and press "
"the LEFT mouse button, the Main Map View will change to center on it.\n"
"\n"
"If you push the mouse pointer to any of the edges of the screen, the "
"Main Map View will SCROLL in the direction of the mouse pointer.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"These buttons ROTATE the Main Map View in either direction.  These do "
"NOT affect the Overview Map.\n"
"\n"
"These buttons ZOOM the Main Map View to one of three levels: far, "
"medium and close.  After you press Zoom In, click on the part of the "
"city you want to zoom in on (zooming out is automatic).  You can make "
"changes to your city at any zoom level."
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Il existe plusieurs façons de changer de vue.\n"
"\n"
"Pointez un endroit de la Vue Générale avec votre souris et appuyez sur "
"le bouton GAUCHE, ce point devient le centre de la carte principale.\n"
"\n"
"Amenez le pointeur de la souris en dehors des bords de la carte, elle "
"DEFILE dans la direction du pointeur.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
" Ces boutons impriment une ROTATION à la Vue Principale dans toutes les "
"directions sans qu'elle soit affectée.\n"
"\n"
"Ces boutons AGRANDISSENT la Vue Principale à trois niveaux: loin, moyen "
"et près. Vous pouvez modifier votre cité dans ces trois niveaux."

msgctxt "help/64/0"
msgid "The Basics (Part I)"
msgstr "Les Bases (Partie I)"

msgctxt "help/64/1"
msgid ""
"We'll get building right away, but first you need to know some basics.\n"
"\n"
"FIRST, building a city costs money, which is counted in Roman coins "
"called DENARII.  The top right corner of the screen shows you how many "
"Denarii you have at all times, so watch it while building to make sure "
"you don't run out!\n"
"\n"
"Also, the cost for any buildings or actions you select is shown in the "
"small display between the banks of icons.\n"
"\n"
"You will spend more Denarii to maintain your city, and you will MAKE "
"Denarii by building successful HOUSES and BUSINESSES -- but we'll "
"explain that later."
msgstr ""
"Nous allons commencer à construire mais il vous faut connaître des "
"bases.\n"
"\n"
"PRIMO, la construction d'une cité est chère, elle se compte en monnaie "
"Romaine appelée les DENIERS. Le coin supérieur gauche de l'écran "
"indique l'état de vos finances, surveillez-le pendant la construction "
"pour ne pas vous ruiner!\n"
"\n"
"Le coût de chaque construction ou action sélectionnée est indiqué dans "
"le petit écran entre les banques d'icônes\n"
"\n"
"Vous dépenserez beaucoup de Deniers à entretenir votre cité, vous "
"GAGNEREZ des Deniers en construisant des MAISONS et des INDUSTRIES -- "
"nous l'expliquerons plus tard."

msgctxt "help/65/0"
msgid "The Basics (Part II)"
msgstr "Les Bases (Partie II)"

msgctxt "help/65/1"
msgid ""
"SECOND, some buildings you put in your city will CHANGE after you build "
"them.  Some will develop into better (and sometimes larger) versions of "
"themselves, like a small tent growing into a great Palace.  Other will "
"become busier, fancier, or more productive.  In each case, the "
"structure grows because it is given things it needs to improve.  The "
"flipside is that when buildings do not have what they need, they may "
"shrink, and even disappear entirely!"
msgstr ""
"SECONDO, certains immeubles construits dans la ville EVOLUENT. Ils "
"peuvent devenir une meilleure (parfois plus grande) version "
"d'eux-mêmes, une petite tente peut devenir un grand palais. D'autres "
"deviennent plus actives, agréables ou productives. Dans chaque cas, "
"l'infrastructure grandit car certaines choses doivent s'améliorer. "
"L'ennuyeux est que si les édifices subissent un manque, ils peuvent "
"rétrécir et même disparaître entièrement."

msgctxt "help/66/0"
msgid "Your Friend, the Query Panel"
msgstr "Votre ami, le Conseil"

msgctxt "help/66/1"
msgid ""
"QUERY lets you find out how different structures in the city are doing. "
" Click on the Query button, then select any button or building for "
"information and on-line help. None of the regular game commands work in "
"Query Mode. To exit this mode, click again on the Query icon.\n"
"\n"
"(You can also query any button or building AT ANY TIME by pointing to "
"it and pressing the RIGHT mouse button.)\n"
"\n"
"When you query a building, the Query panel has several modes; for now, "
"leave it in GENERAL mode (indicated by the bottom-left icon).  This "
"mode tells you whether the building is growing or shrinking, and the "
"most important issue (if any) affecting its growth.  You will learn "
"about those issues in time.  For now, just remember that any time you "
"want any information about something in your city, USE THE QUERY PANEL."
msgstr ""
"Le CONSEIL vous renseigne sur l'état des structures de la cité. Cliquez "
"sur ?, puis sélectionnez un bouton ou un édifice pour obtenir des "
"informations et une aide en ligne. Aucune des commandes du jeu ne "
"fonctionne en mode Conseil. Pour quitter ce mode, cliquez de nouveau "
"sur la touche ?.\n"
"\n"
"(Pour vous renseigner sur un bouton ou un immeuble A TOUT MOMENT "
"pointez cet élément et cliquez sur le bouton DROIT de la souris.)\n"
"\n"
"Pour un immeuble, le Conseil a plusieurs modes; pour l'instant, "
"laissez-le en mode GENERAL (l'icône en bas et à gauche). Il indique si "
"l'immeuble grandit ou rétrécit, et le problème le plus important (le "
"cas échéant) affectant sa croissance. Ces problèmes seront expliqués en "
"temps voulu. Pour l'instant, pensez que dès que vous voulez une "
"information, il y a le CONSEIL."

msgctxt "help/67/0"
msgid "Enough Talk -- Let's Build!"
msgstr "Assez Parlé -- Construisons!"

msgctxt "help/67/1"
msgid ""
"Without further ado, you will start building houses.  When you select "
"the next page of this tutorial, you will be taken to the city view.  "
"There you can select these two icons (in addition to the "
"already-mentioned View and Query icons):\n"
"\n"
"HOUSING lets you place tents.  With the proper surroundings, these will "
"grow and change into fancier types of dwelling.  Without them, they may "
"wither and disappear.\n"
"\n"
"CLEAR AREA lets you remove houses or other structures from the City.  "
"Most of them turn to rubble when cleared, which you can then remove by "
"clearing it again.  Rubble is also cleared for you when you build on "
"it.  You have to pay to clear areas.\n"
"\n"
"To use either icon on a single square of the map, just select the "
"appropriate icon, point to the square and click."
msgstr ""
"Sans plus attendre, commençons à construire. La prochaine page de ce "
"tutorial est une vue de la cité. Là, vous pouvez choisir deux icônes "
"(en plus de celles déjà mentionnées).\n"
"\n"
"\"Habitat\" permet de placer des tentes. Dans un environnement adapté, "
"ces immeubles grandissent et se transforment en résidences agréables. "
"Sinon, ils s'étiolent et disparaissent.\n"
"\n"
"\"Nettoyer zone\" permet de retirer des maisons ou autres structures de "
"la cité. Dans ce cas, la plupart deviennent des ruines que vous pouvez "
"enlever en nettoyant ou en construisant par dessus. Vous devez payer "
"pour déblayer des ruines.\n"
"\n"
"Pour utiliser une de ces icônes sur un carré, sélectionnez l'icône, "
"pointez le carré et cliquez."

msgctxt "help/68/0"
msgid "Enough Talk -- Let's Build! (cont..)"
msgstr "Assez Parlé -- Construisons! (suite)"

msgctxt "help/68/1"
msgid ""
"Both of these commands let you build (or destroy) on several squares at "
"once.  Just click on one square and HOLD the mouse button down, and "
"then DRAG the mouse to another square -- a rectangle of squares between "
"those two points will be filled with tents, or cleared, as requested.  "
"For other structures, this will let you build a road, wall, or aqueduct "
"between the two points.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Once you select an icon, you can use it as much as you like, until you "
"select another one.\n"
"\n"
"Now turn the page and start experimenting with these icons.  When "
"you're ready for more, wait for the timer to count down to zero, or "
"just press this Button."
msgstr ""
"Ces deux commandes permettent de construire (ou détruire) plusieurs "
"carrés à la fois. Cliquez sur un carré, maintenez le bouton de la "
"souris enfoncé, puis glissez-la vers un autre carré -- le rectangle "
"compris entre ces deux points sera rempli ou détruit, selon l'option. "
"Cette méthode permet aussi la construction d'une route, d'un mur ou "
"d'un aqueduc entre les deux points.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
" Dès la sélection de l'icône, elle peut être utilisée indéfiniment "
"jusqu'au choix d'une autre.\n"
"\n"
"Maintenant, tournez la page et commencez à tester ces icônes. Attendez "
"ensuite la fin du décompte pour en savoir plus, ou appuyez sur ce bouton."

msgctxt "help/69/0"
msgid "Okay, So What's Going On?"
msgstr "OK, que se passe-t-il?"

msgctxt "help/69/1"
msgid ""
"When you built houses, you saw that they DIDN'T actually grow much "
"larger; they stayed as small tents.  Some of them may have even "
"disappeared soon after you built them.  Since growing houses into "
"beautiful mansions is one of your main jobs as Governor, you'll "
"probably want to know why.  The important thing to remember about "
"houses is that there are only two things that stop them from growing.  "
"Either --\n"
"\n"
"A) the LAND VALUE in their area is too low,\n"
"\n"
"  -- OR --\n"
"\n"
"B) they are missing something that they NEED.\n"
"\n"
"(If you QUERIED your houses, you may have found some of this out already.)"
msgstr ""
"Lorsque vous avez construit les maisons, elles n'ont PAS grandi; elles "
"sont restées de petites tentes. Certaines d'entre elles ont même "
"disparu peu de temps après leur construction. Faire que les petites "
"maisons deviennent de somptueuses demeures étant votre tâche "
"principale, vous voulez certainement savoir pourquoi. Il est important "
"de savoir que deux choses seulement peuvent stopper la croissance d'une "
"maison : \n"
"\n"
" -- Soit --\n"
"\n"
"A) Le COUT FONCIER de cette zone est trop bas,\n"
"\n"
"  -- Soit --\n"
"\n"
"B) Il leur manque une chose dont elles ont BESOIN \n"
"\n"
"(Si vous avez QUESTIONNE vos maisons, si savez déjà de quoi il s'agît.)"

msgctxt "help/70/0"
msgid "What is Land Value?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que le coût foncier ?"

msgctxt "help/70/1"
msgid ""
"LAND VALUE is a number between 0 and 64 that is given to every square "
"on the city map.  Everything you place on the map affects the value of "
"the land surrounding it.  For example, if you build a Coliseum in the "
"city, it boosts nearby land values because entertainment is good for "
"your city.  It's also something that houses like to be near, and that's "
"important because LAND VALUE DETERMINES HOW LARGE A HOUSE CAN GROW.  "
"The higher the land value is in a square, the larger and fancier a "
"house built there will become.  Some other buildings (like temples and "
"fountains) also improve in high land value, but houses are affected the "
"most (and are most important).\n"
"\n"
"Most things you build add to land values (why build something that "
"hurts your city?); items that result from disaster -- fire, rubble, "
"disease -- actively LOWER land values.  A few structures -- mainly "
"those related to industry and security -- will LIMIT land values in the "
"areas around them.  This is because, just as you won't find mansions "
"built right next to factories, your city won't produce palaces right "
"next to these necessary, but less-than-dazzling buildings.\n"
"\n"
"You can learn the land value of a square by QUERYING it."
msgstr ""
"Le COUT FONCIER est un nombre compris entre 0 et 64 et attribué à "
"chaque carré de la carte. Chaque élément placé sur la carte affecte la "
"valeur de la terre voisine. Par exemple, si vous bâtissez un Colisée "
"dans la ville, le prix des terres voisines monte, les loisirs étant "
"bons pour votre ville. C'est un bon voisinage pour les maisons et c'est "
"important car LE COUT FONCIER DETERMINE LA TAILLE DES MAISONS.  Plus le "
"coût foncier d'un carré est élevé, plus la maison construite deviendra "
"grande et belle. D'autres constructions (les temples et les fontaines) "
"valorisent le coût foncier, mais les maisons sont plus affectées (et "
"sont plus importantes).\n"
"\n"
"La plupart des constructions valorisent la terre (pourquoi construire "
"pour nuire à la ville?); les conséquences des désastres -- feu, ruines, "
"maladie -- DIMINUENT le prix des terres.  Quelques structures -- "
"surtout celles relatives à l'industrie et la sécurité -- LIMITENT la "
"valeur des terres voisines. C'est pourquoi, tout comme on ne trouve pas "
"de manoir près d'une manufacture, votre ville ne produira pas de palais "
"près de ces constructions nécessaires mais peu reluisantes.\n"
"\n"
"Pour connaître le coût d'un carré de terre, vous devez le QUESTIONNER."

msgctxt "help/71/0"
msgid "Making Things Clear -- Color Overlays"
msgstr "Clarifier les choses -- Calques"

msgctxt "help/71/1"
msgid ""
"To get a better idea of how land values -- and other issues affecting "
"your city -- work, you can use the Color Overlay maps.  These are "
"color-coded reports that appear on top of the Overview Map, and can be "
"displayed on the Main Map View by pressing the Map Legend button.  This "
"button also explains what the colors in an Overlay mean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Call up a Color Overlay by clicking on this window, and selecting a "
"report from the menu that appears.  There are Color Overlay reports for "
"almost every issue affecting the city.\n"
"\n"
"Now let's take a look at the second thing that limits a house's growth "
"-- when it NEEDS something."
msgstr ""
"Pour avoir une meilleure idée du fonctionnement du coût foncier -- et "
"autres problèmes affectant votre cité --, vous pouvez utiliser les "
"cartes colorées. Ce sont des rapports avec codes de couleurs qui "
"apparaissent sur la carte principale lorsque vous pressez le bouton "
"Légende. Ce bouton explique aussi la signification des couleurs. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Pour appeler un rapport coloré, cliquez sur cette fenêtre et "
"sélectionnez-le dans le menu qui apparaît. Il existe un rapport pour "
"chaque problème affectant la cité.\n"
"\n"
"Maintenant, jetons un oeil sur le deuxième facteur de limitation de "
"croissance -- la maison a BESOIN de quelque chose."

msgctxt "help/72/0"
msgid "Water, the first Housing Need"
msgstr "L'eau, le besoin primordial"

msgctxt "help/72/1"
msgid ""
"Houses need many things to reach their full potential; the purpose of "
"most of the structures you build in the city is to provide for those "
"needs.  The first, most important need these people have is for a "
"source of WATER.  Fortunately, you have many ways to give them water -- "
"and TWO types of water to give.\n"
"\n"
"The most important type of water is WATER SUPPLY, which is what people "
"can actually use.  The second type is PIPE ACCESS, which gives water to "
"OTHER BUILDINGS.\n"
"\n"
"WELLS are a primitive Water Supply.  Building one will let houses grow "
"only SO FAR; they will need a better Water Supply to expand further.\n"
"\n"
"RIVERS are also a primitive water supply, but naturally you can't build "
"them.\n"
"\n"
"When built next to a River, RESERVOIRS provide a better Water Supply "
"for people in a small area, but more importantly they provide PIPE "
"ACCESS to buildings like --"
msgstr ""
"Pour atteindre leur potentiel, il faut beaucoup de choses aux maisons; "
"le but des structures construites dans la ville est de répondre à ces "
"besoins. Le premier besoin des gens, et le plus important, est une "
"source d'EAU. Heureusement, vous pouvez les approvisionner en eau de "
"plusieurs façons -- et leur donner DEUX types d'eau.\n"
"\n"
"Le type le plus important est l'EAU POTABLE, utilisée couramment par le "
"peuple. Le second est l'ADDUCTION, qui donne de l'eau aux AUTRES "
"IMMEUBLES.\n"
"\n"
"Le PUITS est un point d'eau primitif. Sa construction permet une "
"croissance LIMITEE; il faut ensuite une meilleure adduction pour la "
"croissance.\n"
"\n"
"La RIVIERE est aussi un point primitif mais, naturellement, vous ne "
"pouvez pas la construire.\n"
"\n"
"Construit près d'une rivière, le RESERVOIR offre un bon point d'eau "
"pour les habitants d'une petite zone mais, plus important, ils "
"fournissent une ADDUCTION aux immeubles comme --"

msgctxt "help/73/0"
msgid "Water (cont..)"
msgstr "L'eau (suite)"

msgctxt "help/73/1"
msgid ""
"FOUNTAINS, which turn Pipe Access into Water Supply for a good-sized "
"area, and AQUEDUCTS that connect two reservoirs together, so that you "
"can build a reservoir that provides water far from a river.  You can "
"connect only five reservoirs together in this way, and each one will "
"give less supply and access than the last.\n"
"\n"
"This picture demonstrates how the different water structures work.  The "
"blue, red and purple areas show which squares have water supply, pipe "
"access, or both, respectively.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Now try to give water to your houses.  When one of these structures is "
"properly set up to provide water, you will see the water.  You can also "
"check on an area's water status by Querying it, or by calling up the "
"WATER Color Overlay.  All water structures are available through the "
"Water icon."
msgstr ""
"les FONTAINES, qui transforment l'adduction d'eau en alimentation pour "
"une zone importante, les AQUEDUCS qui relient les réservoirs ensemble, "
"de telle sorte que vous pouvez construire un réservoir qui fournit de "
"l'eau loin d'une rivière. Vous ne pouvez relier que cinq réservoirs de "
"cette façon, chacun donnant moins d'eau et d'accès que le précédent.\n"
"Cette image montre le fonctionnement des différentes structures "
"aquatiques. Les zones bleue, rouge et pourpre indiquent respectivement "
"les carrés alimentés en eau, adduction ou les deux.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Essayez maintenant d'amener l'eau à vos maisons. Lorsqu'une des "
"structures est correctement installée pour amener de l'eau, l'eau "
"apparaît. Vous pouvez également vérifier l'approvisionnement en eau "
"d'une zone en la questionnant, ou en appelant le rapport coloré de l'EAU."

msgctxt "help/74/0"
msgid "Forum and Roads"
msgstr "Forum et Routes"

msgctxt "help/74/1"
msgid ""
"To grow further, your houses will want access to other areas of the "
"city and the services they provide.  For this, they need access to "
"ROADS.  Houses don't need to be directly on a road in order to use "
"them, but they shouldn't be too far away from one.  You can join two "
"points with a road by clicking-and-dragging the mouse as you do for "
"Aqueducts.\n"
"\n"
"The first thing houses will use roads for is to get to a FORUM.  People "
"like Forums because they are good gathering places; YOU will like "
"forums because they collect POPULATION TAX from your houses.  "
"Population Tax is one of your two sources of income, so you'll want to "
"give forum access to all your houses.  Now you can only build one type "
"of forum, the Aventine; but when your city has grown large enough, "
"you'll be able to build larger and more effective ones.\n"
"\n"
"When you build a forum, make sure it's right next to a road.  You'll "
"see why soon after you build one; as long as you have some houses in "
"your city, that's when the forum will produce its first WALKER."
msgstr ""
"Pour croître, les maisons doivent accéder aux autres zones de la cité "
"et aux services qu'elles offrent. Pour cela, il faut des ROUTES. Les "
"maisons n'ont pas à donner directement sur la route pour l'utiliser, "
"mais elles ne doivent pas en être trop éloignées. Pour joindre deux "
"points par une route, cliquez et glissez la souris comme pour les "
"aqueducs.\n"
"\n"
"La première destination des routes est le Forum. Le peuple aime les "
"Forums car ce sont de bons lieux de rassemblement; vous aimerez les "
"Forums car ils collectent la TAXE DE POPULATION de vos maisons. La Taxe "
"de Population est une de vos deux sources de revenus, toutes vos "
"maisons doivent donc avoir accès aux Forums. Pour l'instant, vous ne "
"pouvez construire qu'un seul type de Forum, l'Aventin; quand votre cité "
"sera assez développée, vous pourrez en construire de plus grands et "
"plus efficaces.\n"
"\n"
"Lorsque vous construisez un Forum, faites-le auprès d'une route. Vous "
"verrez pourquoi juste après en avoir construit un; si votre cité "
"possède des maisons, le Forum produira son premier MARCHEUR."

msgctxt "help/75/0"
msgid "Forum and Roads (cont..)"
msgstr "Forum et Routes (suite)"

msgctxt "help/75/1"
msgid ""
"Walkers are little people that forge links between buildings in your "
"city; in this case the walker is called a Forum Clerk.  You actually "
"see walkers wander around your city, providing a link (in this case, "
"Forum Access) to every area of the map they pass by.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"However, walkers can only walk so far before they are replaced with a "
"new one, and they make random turns at each crossing they reach.  So "
"you must build a network of roads large enough for walkers to get "
"around quickly and easily, but not so large that they get confused and "
"wander aimlessly.\n"
"\n"
"If you display the Cover Overlay called \"Tax Coverage\" (because forum "
"access equals tax coverage), you can see what areas are linked to "
"forums.  Note that areas around forums ALWAYS have forum access.  "
"Return to your city now to give your houses road access, and place a "
"forum somewhere on those roads."
msgstr ""
"Les marcheurs sont de petits personnages qui forment des liens entre "
"les immeubles de votre cité; dans ce cas, le marcheur est appelé Commis "
"du Forum. Vous voyez des marcheurs errer autour de votre cité, "
"constituant un lien (appelé dans ce cas Accès au Forum) entre chaque "
"zone traversée de la carte.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
" Cependant, le marcheur peut seulement marcher jusqu'à ce qu'il soit "
"remplacé par un nouveau, il tourne aléatoirement à chaque carrefour. "
"Construisez un réseau routier assez grand pour que les marcheurs se "
"déplacent rapidement et facilement, mais pas trop pour qu'ils ne soient "
"pas embarrassés et qu'ils n'errent pas sans but.\n"
"\n"
"Si vous affichez le calque appelé \"recouvrement des taxes\" (impliqué "
"par l'accès au Forum), vous pouvez voir les zones reliées au Forum. "
"Notez que les zones jouxtant un Forum y ont TOUJOURS accès. Revenez à "
"la cité pour donner des accès routiers à vos maisons, et placez un "
"Forum sur ces routes."

msgctxt "help/76/0"
msgid "Internal Security"
msgstr "Sécurité Interne"

msgctxt "help/76/1"
msgid ""
"There are two types of security that houses need.  INTERNAL Security "
"protects houses from threats within the city.  EXTERNAL Security "
"protects against threats from outside the city.  The Security icon "
"builds these structures:\n"
"\n"
"PRAEFECTURES produce walkers called \"Vigiles\" who wander around the "
"city watching for fires, rioters or invaders. If they find one, they "
"try to get rid of it.\n"
"\n"
"BARRACKS produce walkers called \"soldiers,\" who keep a look out for "
"rioters or enemy barbarians attacking the city, and will attack and try "
"to defeat any they find.  They are much better at this combat than "
"vigiles.\n"
"\n"
"Like any structure that produces walkers, both buildings need to be "
"built NEXT TO ROADS.  Any areas that either a Vigile or Soldier "
"regularly walks past will receive Internal Security."
msgstr ""
"Les maisons nécessitent deux types de sécurité. La sécurité INTERNE "
"protège la maison des menaces de la cité. La sécurité EXTERNE protège "
"des menaces extérieures à la cité. L'icône Sécurité construit ces "
"infrastructures:\n"
"\n"
"Les PREFECTURES génèrent des marcheurs appelés \"Vigiles\" qui errent "
"dans les rues en surveillant les incendies, émeutiers ou envahisseurs. "
"S'ils en trouvent, ils vous en débarrassent.\n"
"\n"
"Les CASERNES génèrent des marcheurs appelés \"Soldats\" qui ont l'oeil "
"sur les émeutiers ou les barbares ennemis qui attaquent la cité; s'ils "
"les trouvent, ils les attaquent et tentent de les vaincre.\n"
"\n"
"Comme toute infrastructure produisant des marcheurs, ces deux "
"constructions doivent se faire PRES DES ROUTES. Toute zone dans "
"laquelle est passée un Vigile ou un Soldat reçoit une sécurité interne."

msgctxt "help/77/0"
msgid "External Security"
msgstr "Sécurité Externe"

msgctxt "help/77/1"
msgid ""
"For external security, you can put a WALL around your city and add "
"TOWERS to strengthen it.  A Wall will help protect the city from "
"barbarian invaders, though barbarians will eventually be able to knock "
"down any wall.  Towers provide one more line of defense, as they will "
"produce Soldiers when an enemy is near.  RIVERS also act as walls, but "
"not if you build Roads over them.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Your citizens want to feel secure, but as mentioned earlier, housing "
"located too near to any security structure will be LIMITED in its "
"growth.\n"
"\n"
"Return to your sample city and add a praefecture or two, plus a "
"barracks.  Make sure they're not too close to your houses, but that "
"they have road access to them.  Add a wall around your city if you like "
"(if you want to spend the money).  Use the SECURITY Color Overlay to "
"see which areas have been secured. "
msgstr ""
"Pour la sécurité externe, entourez la cité d'un MUR et ajoutez des "
"TOURS pour le renforcer. Le Mur protège la cité même s'il peut être "
"démoli. Les tours produisent des soldats lorsqu'un ennemi approche. Les "
"RIVIERES offrent également protection, sauf si une route les traverse.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
" Vos citoyens doivent se sentir en sécurité mais, comme il fut dit "
"auparavant, la croissance de toute construction effectuée près d'une "
"zone de sécurité sera LIMITEE.\n"
"\n"
"Retournez à votre exemple et ajoutez une ou deux préfectures et une "
"caserne. Assurez-vous qu'elles ne soient pas trop près de vos maisons, "
"mais qu'une route en assure l'accès. Si vous le désirez, ajoutez un mur "
"autour de la Cité (si vous voulez dépenser). Pour vérifier les zones "
"sécurisées, servez-vous du calque SECURITE. "

msgctxt "help/78/0"
msgid "The Forum Screen"
msgstr "L'Ecran Forum"

msgctxt "help/78/1"
msgid ""
"Aside from the Forums you build in your city for your people to use, "
"you have a Forum of your own that YOU can use.  It contains advisors "
"and areas that help you control your city's services and see how well "
"the city is doing.\n"
"\n"
"To reach your Forum, click on the Go to Forum Icon.\n"
"\n"
"You click on the people and objects here to access them.  (You can also "
"use the menu at the bottom of the screen.)  There are nine areas in the "
"Forum, seven of which are used in this tutorial.  We'll discuss three "
"of them now -- you can discover the rest."
msgstr ""
"A part des Forums construits pour les habitants de la Cité, vous "
"disposez d'un Forum PARTICULIER. Il contient des conseillers et des "
"zones vous aidant à contrôler les services de votre cité et si tout s'y "
"passe bien.\n"
"\n"
"Pour rejoindre votre Forum, cliquez sur l'icône Aller au Forum.\n"
"\n"
"Cliquez sur les gens et objets présents pour y accéder. (Vous pouvez "
"également utiliser le menu du bas de l'écran.) Le Forum comprend neuf "
"zones, sept d'entre elles sont présentes dans ce tutorial. Nous "
"parlerons de trois d'entre elles dès maintenant -- vous pourrez "
"découvrir les autres."

msgctxt "help/79/0"
msgid "Maintenance and the Plebeian Tribune"
msgstr "L'entretien et le Tribun de la Plèbe"

msgctxt "help/79/1"
msgid ""
"The Plebeian Tribune directs the work force of Plebs that are assigned "
"to specific jobs in your city -- fire prevention, roads, water and "
"walls.  (A set amount are assigned to construction; if you don't "
"provide enough welfare for even them, you won't be able to build!)  You "
"can use the arrows to move the plebs between jobs, and to change the "
"amount spent on their welfare (which changes how many plebs you have).\n"
"\n"
"As a city grows, the numbers you need for each job will grow.  If you "
"end up with too few plebs for a job, a warning will appear on the Menu "
"Bar, giving you some time to go the Plebeian Tribune to fix things.  If "
"you don't, disaster may strike!\n"
"\n"
"Since new plebs take time to appear, you should plan any welfare "
"changes ahead of time.  When expanding your city, keep extra plebs on "
"hand for each job."
msgstr ""
"Le Tribun de la Plèbe dirige les travailleurs plébéiens assignés aux "
"tâches spécifiques de la cité -- prévention des incendies, routes, eau "
"et murs. (Un nombre donné est assigné à la construction; si vous ne "
"donnez pas assez de confort, vous serez incapable de construire!) "
"Servez-vous des flèches pour déplacer les plébéiens de tâche en tâche "
"et pour modifier les sommes allouées à leur confort (qui varient avec "
"le nombre de plébéiens).\n"
"\n"
"A mesure de la croissance de la cité, le nombre nécessaire pour chaque "
"tâche augmente. Si vous avez trop peu de plébéiens pour une tâche, un "
"message apparaît sur la Barre de Menu, vous donnant du temps pour aller "
"voir le Tribu de la Plèbe et arranger les choses. Si vous ne le faites "
"pas, un désastre peut frapper!\n"
"\n"
"L'apparition de nouveaux plébéiens prend un certain temps, vous devez "
"donc planifier le changements de leur niveau de vie à l'avance. Lorsque "
"la cité se développe, gardez une réserve de plébéiens pour chaque tâche."

msgctxt "help/80/0"
msgid "Taxes and The Treasurer"
msgstr "Les Taxes et le Trésorier"

msgctxt "help/80/1"
msgid ""
"The Treasurer keeps tracks of your finances, and lets you set the tax "
"rates for your city.  You collect two types of taxes:\n"
"\n"
"POPULATION TAX, which comes from houses, and\n"
"\n"
"INDUSTRIAL TAX, which comes from businesses.\n"
"\n"
"You can set a different rate for each of these taxes.  If you raise a "
"tax rate, you will get more money, but you risk angering your "
"population and decreasing productivity."
msgstr ""
"Le Trésorier enregistre vos finances et permet de définir les impôts de "
"la cité. Vous collectez deux types de taxes :\n"
"\n"
"La Taxe Populaire, qui provient des maisons, et\n"
"\n"
"La Taxe Industrielle, qui émane des manufactures.\n"
"\n"
"Chaque taux de taxe peut être défini séparément. Si vous augmentez un "
"taux, vous aurez plus d'argent mais vous risquez de mécontenter la "
"population et de faire baisser la productivité."

msgctxt "help/81/0"
msgid "Ratings and the Oracle"
msgstr "Les Indices et l'Oracle"

msgctxt "help/81/1"
msgid ""
"The Oracle screen shows your performance as COLUMNS that rise as you do "
"better.  The two columns on the right -- PROSPERITY AND CULTURE -- are "
"the only ones measured in a city-building-only game.  In a full game "
"(which includes the Province Level and optional Battles), all four "
"ratings (the previous two, plus PEACE and EMPIRE) are used to determine "
"when you deserve to get a PROMOTION to a tougher, more challenging city.\n"
"\n"
"When you want to learn how your city can improve, click on the BOXES "
"below each column for advice.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Now go to the forum, and check out these three areas.  Make sure to:\n"
"\n"
"+ Increase your spending on pleb welfare, and assign plebs where they "
"are needed (you will be doing a lot of building, so add extra ones to "
"Fire Prevention!)\n"
"\n"
"+ Check out your cash balances, and adjust your tax rates if you want "
"(but be prepared for the consequences!)"
msgstr ""
"L''Oracle indique vos performances en COLONNES qui montent avec vos "
"résultats. Les deux colonnes de droite -- PROSPERITE et CULTURE -- sont "
"les seules mesures Mode Cité Seulement. Dans le jeu complet (qui inclut "
"le niveau provincial et les batailles optionnelles), les quatre indices "
"(les deux précédents, plus PAIX et EMPIRE) sont utilisés pour "
"déterminer si vous méritez une PROMOTION pour gérer une cité plus dure "
"et compétitive.\n"
"\n"
"Pour savoir comment votre cité peut se développer, demandez un avis en "
"cliquant sur les BOITES situées sous chaque colonne.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Maintenant, allez au Forum et vérifiez ces trois éléments. Assurez vous "
"de :\n"
"\n"
"+ Accroître vos dépenses pour le bien-être de la Plèbe, si nécessaire "
"(vous allez construire de nombreux immeubles, alors attention aux "
"risques d'incendie!)\n"
"\n"
"+ Vérifiez votre trésorerie, et réglez vos taux d'impôts si vous le "
"désirez (mais soyez prêt à en subir les conséquences!)"

msgctxt "help/82/0"
msgid "What Else Can I Build?"
msgstr "Que puis-je construire d'autre ?"

msgctxt "help/82/1"
msgid ""
"Houses have many other needs that can be fulfilled by other buildings "
"-- some are very important for every citizen, while others are only "
"required for the elite who live in villas and palaces.  All of these "
"buildings increase the land values around them.  The following buttons "
"let you build these structures:\n"
"\n"
"SANITATION lets you build Baths and Hospitals.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The WORSHIP button lets you build three sizes of religious structures.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The ENTERTAINMENT button lets you build Theaters, Arenas and Circuses."
msgstr ""
"Les maisons ont de nombreux autres besoins qui peuvent être satisfaits "
"avec d'autres constructions -- certains sont très importants pour "
"chaque citoyen, alors que les autres sont destinés à l'élite vivant "
"dans les villas et les palais. Les boutons suivants permettent les "
"constructions suivantes :\n"
"\n"
"SANTE permet de construire des thermes et des hôpitaux.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"LIEU-SAINT permet de construire trois types de structures religieuses.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"LOISIR permet de construire des théâtres, des Arènes et des Cirques."

msgctxt "help/83/0"
msgid "What Else...? (cont..)"
msgstr "Que puis-je...? (suite)"

msgctxt "help/83/1"
msgid ""
"The EDUCATION button lets you build the Grammaticus, Rhetor and "
"Library. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The AMENITIES button lets you build Gardens and Plazas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The INDUSTRY button lets you build Markets, and eight kinds of Business.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"You can learn about each of these buildings by referring to the On-Line "
"Help or the Game Manual.  Now try them out for a while, and then come "
"back here for some final tips."
msgstr ""
"EDUCATION permet la construction d'écoles de Grammaire et de Rhétorique "
"et des Bibliothèques.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"AGREMENT vous permet de construire des Jardins et des Places.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"INDUSTRIE permet de construire des Marchés et huit types de "
"manufactures.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Pour tout apprendre sur ces constructions, reportez-vous à l'aide en "
"ligne ou au manuel du jeu. Maintenant, exercez vous un peu et revenez "
"pour d'autres conseils finaux."

msgctxt "help/84/0"
msgid "End of Tutorial"
msgstr "Fin du Tutorial"

msgctxt "help/84/1"
msgid ""
"In conclusion, follow these basic guidelines when expanding your city:\n"
"\n"
"- Increase your profitability by building INDUSTRY.\n"
"\n"
"- QUERY your houses regularly, and try your best to give them what they "
"want.  Keep a particular eye on the GROWTH RATES listed there.\n"
"\n"
"- Change your tax and conscription rates carefully, or else risk "
"angering your population and industries.\n"
"\n"
"- Maintain a cash reserve, so you are always prepared to deal with an "
"emergency.\n"
"\n"
"- Finally, remember that the city level is only PART of the Caesar II "
"experience.  Try starting a new game with the Campaign option ON.\n"
"\n"
"Hail, Caesar!"
msgstr ""
"En conclusion, suivez ces règles de base pour développer votre cité :\n"
"\n"
"- Augmentez la rentabilité en construisant des INDUSTRIES.\n"
"\n"
"- Questionnez régulièrement vos maisons et faites votre possible pour "
"leur donner ce dont elles ont besoin. Gardez l'oeil sur les TAUX DE "
"CROISSANCE indiqués.\n"
"\n"
"- Modifiez prudemment vos taux d'imposition et de conscription. Vous "
"risqueriez de mécontenter la population.\n"
"\n"
"- Gardez une réserve de trésorerie afin d'être toujours prêt à traiter "
"en urgence.\n"
"\n"
"- Enfin, n'oubliez pas que le niveau local n'est qu'une PARTIE de "
"l'expérience CAESAR II. Essayez de commencer un jeu en activant "
"l'option Campagne.\n"
"\n"
"Avé, César!"

