msgctxt "help/95/0"
msgid "Money"
msgstr "L'Argent"

msgctxt "help/95/1"
msgid ""
"Money is what makes everything in the game happen. It pays for "
"construction, labor, and defense, and it appeases the Emperor. The unit "
"of currency in Imperial Rome is the Denarius -- the plural (and "
"hopefully you will have more than one) is Denarii. The amount of "
"Denarii you have in your coffers will be displayed at all times in the "
"upper right corner of the City Level and Province Level screens. Your "
"Denarii will be stored in your Religious Buildings, and can be stolen "
"if security is low.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #96Next Page"
msgstr ""
"L'Argent est l'élément qui rend le jeu possible. Il paye les "
"constructions, les ouvriers, la défense et apaise l'Empereur. L'unité "
"monétaire de la Rome Impériale est le Denier. Le montant des Deniers "
"contenus dans vos coffres s'affiche en permanence dans le coin "
"supérieur droit des écrans des modes Cité et Campagne. Vos Deniers sont "
"stockés dans les édifices religieux, ils peuvent être volés quand "
"l'indice de sécurité est bas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Page Précédente# / #96Page suivante"

msgctxt "help/96/0"
msgid "Money (page 2)"
msgstr "L'Argent  (page 2)"

msgctxt "help/96/1"
msgid ""
"You have two sources of income: Population Taxes and Industrial Taxes.\n"
"Population Tax is a percentage of each household's income. Both "
"population size and housing quality determine population tax. The "
"higher quality houses contain people with higher incomes, who pay more "
"taxes. You should work to increase your population and develop your "
"housing to maximize population taxes. Be careful: if you raise taxes "
"too high, people will not want to live in your city, your population "
"may drop, and the public may hold it against you for a long time! \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#95Previous Page# / #97Next Page#"
msgstr ""
"Vous disposez de deux sources de revenus : les taxes Populaire et "
"Industrielle.\n"
"La taxe populaire est un pourcentage du revenu de chaque habitant. Elle "
"est déterminée à la fois par la taille de la population et la qualité "
"de construction qui, si elle est élevée, abrite des gens à fort revenu "
"qui payent plus de taxes. Vous devez travailler à développer la "
"population et l'habitat pour augmenter les revenus des taxes. Veillez "
"cependant à ne pas trop élever le taux des impôts, les gens ne "
"voudraient pas vivre dans votre Cité, la population chuterait et vous "
"en voudrait pour longtemps!\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#95Page Précédente# / #97Page Suivante#"

msgctxt "help/97/0"
msgid "Money (page 3)"
msgstr "L'Argent (page 3)"

msgctxt "help/97/1"
msgid ""
"Industrial Tax is a percentage of the earnings of your businesses, "
"which come from output. Each business in your city will have a number "
"of jars next to it, representing its output. You must maximize output "
"by boosting both supply of raw materials and demand of the population. "
"You should also try to establish a network of trade routes on the "
"Province Level. If you raise industrial tax too high, businesses may "
"collapse.\n"
"Your expenses will include construction costs, Legion wages, Pleb "
"welfare, annual tribute, and your own salary.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#96Previous Page# / #98Next Page#"
msgstr ""
"La taxe industrielle est un pourcentage des gains de vos industries, "
"dus à leur production. Chaque manufacture possède un certain nombre de "
"jarres, représentant sa production. Vous devez encourager la production "
"en augmentant la fourniture de matières premières et la demande de la "
"population. Vous devez aussi établir un réseau de routes commerciales "
"en Mode Campagne. Si la taxe industrielle est trop élevée, les affaires "
"disparaissent.\n"
"Vos dépenses comprennent les coûts de construction, les salaires de la "
"Légion, des Plébéiens, le Tribut annuel et votre propre salaire.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#96Page Précédente# / #98Page Suivante#"

msgctxt "help/98/0"
msgid "Money (page 4)"
msgstr "L'Argent (page 4)"

msgctxt "help/98/1"
msgid ""
"To be successful, you must balance your income and your expenses so "
"that you earn a profit, otherwise you will be unable to afford to "
"enhance your city. Your Prosperity rating will only improve if you can "
"consistently make a profit. A good city will need substantial income "
"from population and industrial taxes to prosper.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#97Previous Page#"
msgstr ""
"Pour réussir, vous devez équilibrer vos revenus et vos dépenses pour "
"faire des bénéfices, sous peine de ne pouvoir développer votre ville. "
"Votre indice de prospérité n'augmente que si vous faites des profits "
"constants. Pour prospérer, une Cité a besoin de revenus substantiels "
"des taxes Populaire et Industrielle.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#97Page Précédente#"

msgctxt "help/99/0"
msgid "Population"
msgstr "Population"

msgctxt "help/99/1"
msgid ""
"Your city's population will grow or shrink based on the conditions of "
"city life. Population is key to your success as a governor -- all "
"ratings are affected to some degree by the city's population -- and you "
"should do all that you can to promote a healthy level of population "
"growth.  This means providing culture, health facilities, education, "
"and other services that enhance urban life. You should also pay special "
"attention to your population tax rate -- a steep tax hike may raise "
"some quick Denarii, but your citizens will resent it, and they do not "
"forget easily.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page#"
msgstr ""
"La population de la Cité augmente ou diminue en fonction des conditions "
"de vie. La population est la clé de votre succès -- elle affecte plus "
"ou moins tous les indices -- et vous devez faire votre possible pour la "
"faire croître sainement. Cela signifie améliorer la vie urbaine par des "
"structures sanitaires, éducatives et autres. Vous devez veiller sur le "
"taux d'imposition -- une augmentation brusque rapporte des Deniers, "
"mais les citoyens le ressentiront et ne l'oublieront pas aisément.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Page Précédente#"

