msgctxt "help/105/0"
msgid "Land Values"
msgstr "Coût Foncier"

msgctxt "help/105/1"
msgid ""
"Land Values determine the extent to which buildings in your city "
"(housing, in particular) will develop or decline. Each map square will "
"have a value ranging from 0 to 64. There are many ever-changing "
"influences which will overlap and work with or against each other to "
"raise or limit the land value of any given square. In other words, it "
"may not always be easy to figure out exactly why any given squareÆs "
"value is higher or lower than another's.\n"
"There are, however, some basic rules to keep in mind when trying to "
"manage land values. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #106Next Page#"
msgstr ""
"Le Coût Foncier détermine si les immeubles de votre cité "
"(principalement l'habitat) vont se développer ou décliner. Chaque carré "
"a une valeur comprise entre 0 et 64. De nombreuses influences "
"fluctuantes interviennent sans cesse pour augmenter ou diminuer cette "
"valeur. En d'autres termes, il est parfois très ardu de comprendre "
"pourquoi la valeur d'un carré de terre est supérieure ou inférieure à "
"un autre.\n"
"Cependant, la gestion du coût foncier obéit à des principes de base.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Page Précédente# / #106Page Suivante#"

msgctxt "help/106/0"
msgid "Land Values (page 2)"
msgstr "Coût Foncier (page 2)"

msgctxt "help/106/1"
msgid ""
"Every structure that you place down will have a radius within which it "
"boosts land values. However, some types of structures will also have "
"the effect of capping, or limiting the value of the land around it. "
"Structures that limit land values are as follows: Barracks, "
"Praefectures, Markets, Businesses, Walls, Gates, and Towers. While "
"these structures are necessary and positive for your city, they just "
"donÆt make good neighbors, so land values near them will always be "
"limited.\n"
"The only influences that will actively reduce land values are rubble, "
"fire, and plague. You would be wise to eliminate these as soon as "
"possible. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#105Previous Page# / #107Next Page#"
msgstr ""
"Chaque infrastructure stimule le coût foncier dans un rayon donné. "
"Cependant certaines d'entre elles ont pour effet de limiter la valeur "
"des terres voisines. Les structures qui limitent le coût foncier sont "
"celles-ci : les Casernes, Préfectures, Marchés, Industries, Murs, "
"Portails et tours. Elles sont certes nécessaires et positives pour "
"votre Cité, mais ont le tort de ne pas être un bon voisinage aussi, "
"elles limitent toujours le coût foncier.\n"
"Les seules vraies mauvaises influences sur le coût foncier sont celles "
"des ruines, du feu et de la peste. Vous devez donc les éliminer au plus "
"vite.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#105Page Précédente# / #107Page Suivante#"

msgctxt "help/107/0"
msgid "Land Values (page 3)"
msgstr "Coût Foncier (page 3)"

msgctxt "help/107/1"
msgid ""
"Other structures -- Bath Houses, Forums, Temples, Entertainment "
"centers, Hospitals, Schools & Libraries, and Amenities -- will have "
"only positive effects on land value. These structures provide valuable "
"services and are a pleasure to live near.\n"
"In addition to the radius of influence that structures exert, some "
"structures also produce walkers, which patrol the streets and provide "
"benefits to any areas they walk past. Praefectures, for example, send "
"out Vigiles which pass a security bonus to any building within a range "
"of three squares that they walk by. Markets send out Market Traders, "
"and Barracks and Towers send out Soldiers. Walkers have a limited "
"lifespan. Keep this in mind as you design your road system. Areas that "
"receive much road traffic will have the highest potential land values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#106Previous Page#"
msgstr ""
"Les autres structures -- Thermes, Forums, Temples, centres de Loisirs, "
"Hôpitaux, Ecoles et Bibliothèques et Agrément -- ont uniquement un "
"effet positif sur le coût foncier. Elles offrent des services "
"appréciables et une meilleure qualité de vie.\n"
"En plus de la zone d'influence exercée, certaines structures produisent "
"des marcheurs qui patrouillent dans les rues et sont profitables aux "
"endroits traversés. Les Préfectures, par exemple, envoient des Vigiles "
"qui offrent un bonus en matière de sécurité dans un rayon de trois "
"carrés dans les zones traversées. Les Marchés envoient des commerçants, "
"les Casernes et les Tours des soldats. Les marcheurs ont une durée de "
"vie limitée. Ne l'oubliez pas lors de la conception de votre réseau "
"routier. Les zones très fréquentées ont un potentiel foncier plus élevé.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#106Page Précédente#"

msgctxt "help/108/0"
msgid "Growth Rates"
msgstr "Taux de croissance"

msgctxt "help/108/1"
msgid ""
"You city will have both an Industrial Growth Rate and a Population "
"Growth Rate, which indicate the trends for development in the city. To "
"check your growth rates, just right click on any structure on the City "
"Level . You should strive to keep both rates as positive as you can. \n"
"Industrial Growth Rate is determined primarily by your Industrial Tax "
"rate. The higher your Industrial taxes, the lower your Industrial "
"Growth Rate will drop. In addition, any sharp increase in Industrial "
"taxes will cause lingering damage your Industrial Growth Rate.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #109Next Page#"
msgstr ""
"Les taux de croissance de la population et des industries de votre Cité "
"indiquent le développement de la ville. Pour vérifier ces indices, "
"cliquez sur une structure en Mode Cité. Vous devez tenter de maintenir "
"ces deux taux aussi positifs que possible.\n"
"Le taux de croissance industriel est avant tout déterminé par votre "
"taxe industrielle. Plus elle est élevée, plus le taux de croissance des "
"entreprises sera bas. De plus, tout accroissement brusque des taxes "
"cause la détérioration tenace du taux de croissance industriel.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Page Précédente# / #109Page Suivante#"

msgctxt "help/109/0"
msgid "Growth Rates (page 2)"
msgstr "Taux de croissance (page 2)"

msgctxt "help/109/1"
msgid ""
"Population Growth Rate is based on your Population Tax Rate, your level "
"of employment, and on the inherent temperament of the people in your "
"Province. If your taxes are low, employment is high, and if your people "
"are happy with your regime, your Population Growth Rate will be high, "
"and you will benefit.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#108Previous Page#"
msgstr ""
"Le taux de croissance de la population est basé sur la Taxe Populaire, "
"le niveau d'emploi, et sur le tempérament propre aux habitants de votre "
"province. Si les taxes sont faibles, l'emploi fort, et si le peuple est "
"heureux avec vous, votre taux de croissance de la population est fort "
"et vous en bénéficiez.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#108Page Précédente#"

