msgid ""
"No history is available for this item. For information on the history "
"of rivers, visit your local library."
msgstr ""
"Aucune information historique sur ce sujet. Pour tout renseignement "
"concernant l'histoire des rivières, pourquoi ne pas aller à la "
"bibliothèque ?"

msgctxt "help/118/0"
msgid "Housing (cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/118/1"
msgid ""
"There are twenty levels of housing, ranging from Hut to Palace. The "
"higher-quality housing attracts more people, who earn higher income and "
"pay more taxes, so it is wise to encourage housing to develop. The "
"development of housing depends on Land Values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#145Previous Page#\n"
"#146Tips# / #147History#"
msgstr ""
"Il existe vingt niveaux de maisons, allant de la hutte au Palais. Les "
"maisons de haute qualité sont plus attractives; le revenu de leurs "
"habitants est plus élevé, ils paient plus d'impôts, il est donc prudent "
"d'encourager le développement de l'habitat. Ce développement dépend du "
"coût foncier.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#145Page Précédente#\n"
"#146Trucs# / #147Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/119/0"
msgid "Roads (cont.)"
msgstr "Routes (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/119/1"
msgid ""
"The cost displayed for road construction is cost per map square of "
"road. You may place a road square by square, or you may hold your mouse "
"button down and drag over the map to lay a length of road. Roads may be "
"built through walls, under aqueducts, and over rivers to form bridges. "
"A few buildings, like hospitals, schools, and libraries.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#38Previous Page#\n"
"#311Tips# / #312History#"
msgstr ""
"Le coût de construction d'une route affiché est exprimé par carré. "
"Placez la route par carré ou par bloc en faisant glisser le curseur de "
"votre souris sur la carte. Elles peuvent traverser les murs, les "
"aqueducs et les rivières pour former des ponts. Elles peuvent passer "
"sous des édifices comme les hôpitaux, les écoles et les bibliothèques.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#38Page Précédente#\n"
"#311Trucs# / #312Histoire#"

