msgctxt "help/144/0"
msgid "Housing"
msgstr "Habitat"

msgctxt "help/144/1"
msgid ""
"This button allows you to place housing in your city. Housing will "
"begin as huts, and will develop into more advanced buildings depending "
"on the Land Value of its location. \n"
"\n"
"#145Help with Housing#\n"
"#146Tips for Housing#\n"
"#147History of Housing#"
msgstr ""
"Ce bouton vous permet de construire des maisons dans votre cité. Au "
"départ, toutes les maisons sont des huttes, elles se développent et "
"s'embellissent en fonction du coût foncier. \n"
"\n"
"#145Aide: L'habitat#\n"
"#146Trucs: L'habitat#\n"
"#147Histoire de l'habitat#"

msgctxt "help/145/0"
msgid "Help with Housing"
msgstr "Aide: L'habitat"

msgctxt "help/145/1"
msgid ""
"People will only move into your city and build nice houses if you "
"provide pleasant areas for them to live.  To place a section of "
"housing, select the Housing button on the control panel and click on "
"the map where you would like to build yoiur houses. All housing will "
"begin as Huts, which will develop and grow only if they get what they "
"need: water, forum access, baths, hospitals, entertainment, and so on. "
"If you fail to provide the basic necessities for your housing, "
"residents will pack up and leave, and your houses will vanish. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#144Previous Page# / #118Next Page#\n"
"#146Tips# / #147History#"
msgstr ""
"Les gens ne viendront construire de belles maisons dans votre ville que "
"si vous leur offrez des endroits agréables. Pour placer des "
"habitations, sélectionnez le bouton Habitat sur le panneau de contrôle "
"et cliquez la zone de la carte à construire. Au départ, toutes les "
"maisons sont des huttes, elles ne se développent que si elles peuvent "
"satisfaire leurs besoins : eau, accès au Forum, bains, hôpitaux, "
"loisirs, etc. Si vous ne fournissez pas le minimum vital, les habitants "
"partent et les maisons disparaissent. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#144Page Précédente# / #118Page Suivante#\n"
"#146Trucs# / #147Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/146/0"
msgid "Tips for Housing"
msgstr "Trucs: L'habitat"

msgctxt "help/146/1"
msgid ""
"There are many different approaches to building successful areas of "
"housing. The one that suits you best will depend on how developed your "
"city is, and what your goals for the new housing are. For instance, if "
"you want to build your industry base, then all your housing needs is "
"some water, road access to your businesses and a forum, and perhaps a "
"few extras to raise land value. If you want to build blocks of the best "
"housing possible, surround them with a road and place all of their "
"needs around them.  More importantly, try to arrange these high-value "
"blocks so that multiple blocks can share the benefits of the same "
"entertainment, education, and so on.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#144Previous Page# / #44Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #147History#"
msgstr ""
"Il existe différentes manières d'urbaniser une zone avec succès. Celle "
"qui vous convient le mieux dépend de votre façon de développer la cité, "
"et de votre objectif pour l'habitat nouveau. Par exemple, pour "
"construire de nouvelles industries de base, il faut de l'eau pour "
"toutes les maisons ainsi qu'un accès routier aux industries et à un "
"Forum, et quelques extras pour augmenter le coût foncier. Pour "
"construire les meilleurs îlots d'habitation possibles, entourez-les "
"d'une route et de ce qui leur est nécessaire. Il est important "
"d'essayer d'agencer ces îlots de forte valeur de telle sorte que "
"plusieurs îlots partagent les mêmes loisirs, les écoles, etc.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#144Page Précédente# / #44Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #147Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/147/0"
msgid "Roman Housing"
msgstr "L'Habitat Romain"

msgctxt "help/147/1"
msgid ""
"At the height of the Empire, the city of Rome sheltered about one "
"million people, a truly staggering population for a city of ancient "
"times.  Less than two out of every ten people in the city could afford "
"to live in a private house, or Domus.  The rest of the population -- "
"more than 800,000 souls -- lived in apartment buildings called Insulae, "
"a Roman invention of necessity.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#148Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"A l'apogée de l'Empire, la ville de Rome abritait près d'un million "
"d'habitants, chiffre stupéfiant pour une cité des temps anciens. Moins "
"de deux habitants de la Cité sur dix pouvaient se permettre de vivre "
"dans une maison, ou Domus. Le reste de la population -- plus de 800 000 "
"individus -- vivaient dans des immeubles appelés Insulae, invention due "
"à la nécessité.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#148Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/148/0"
msgid "Roman Housing (Cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/148/1"
msgid ""
"The Domus was a pleasant dwelling, built as a hollow rectangle one or "
"two stories high, with the living quarters surrounding an inner garden. "
" It could house an extended family of a dozen or more members, plus "
"several dozen more slaves, servants, and close friends.  The wealthiest "
"Romans even had private running water piped into their homes.  \n"
"\n"
"The residents of the Insulae were less fortunate.  These \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#147Previous Page# / #149Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"La Domus était une demeure plaisante, construite comme un rectangle "
"évidé haute d'un ou deux étages, les quartiers résidentiels entourant "
"le jardin intérieur. Elle pouvait abriter une grande famille d'une "
"douzaine de membres voire plus, auxquels venaient s'ajouter plusieurs "
"douzaines d'esclaves ou plus, des servants et des amis proches. Les "
"maisons des Romains les plus riches étaient parfois équipées d'une "
"adduction d'eau.\n"
"\n"
"Les habitants des insulae étaient moins riches.  Ces\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#147Page Précédente# / #149Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/149/0"
msgid "Roman Housing (Cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/149/1"
msgid ""
"buildings were usually at least three stories tall, and some grew as "
"high as seven stories. Each floor held a separate apartment, or "
"cenacula, and each cenacula housed five or six people. The first story "
"of the building was made of stone, but the upper stories used "
"progressively more and more wood, to make them lighter and easier to "
"construct. This also made them flimsier, more prone to collapse, less "
"resistant to the weather, and a major fire hazard. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#148Previous Page# / #150 Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"constructions étaient en général hautes de trois étages, certaines "
"pouvant atteindre sept niveaux. Un appartement séparé, ou cenacula, se "
"trouvait sur chaque palier, et logeait cinq ou six personnes. Le "
"premier étage était construit en pierre, les étages supérieurs "
"employant une proportion croissante de bois pour les rendre plus légers "
"et plus faciles à construire. Ceci les rendait moins solide, plus "
"enclins à l'effondrement, moins résistants aux intempéries et très "
"exposés aux incendies.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#148Page Précédente# / #150 Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/150/0"
msgid "Roman Housing (Cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/150/1"
msgid ""
"The lower apartments were therefore the most desirable and expensive; "
"they were often leased to shopkeepers and artisans as retail space.  "
"The top floor was the most miserable place in the insula to live -- hot "
"in the summer, cold in the winter, and a death trap in the case of "
"collapse or fire.  \n"
"\n"
"So far, archaeological excavations have turned up evidence of Insulae "
"only at Rome and Ostia, Rome's port city.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#149Previous Page# / #151 Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, les appartements du bas étaient plus convoités et chers; ils "
"étaient souvent loués aux marchands et artisans comme point de vente. "
"Le dernier étage était la place la plus misérable pour y vivre -- chaud "
"en été, froid en hiver et piège mortel en cas d'effondrement ou "
"d'incendie.\n"
"\n"
"Les fouilles archéologiques n'ont permis la découverte d'Insulae qu'à "
"Rome et Ostie, le port de Rome.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#149Page Précédente# / #151 Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/151/0"
msgid "Roman Housing (Cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/151/1"
msgid ""
"Provincial towns might have had a few Insulae, but since space wasn't "
"at nearly the premium it was in Rome, most citizens managed to have a "
"Domus, even if only a small one.  \n"
"\n"
"The wealthiest Romans could afford the luxury of a country house, "
"called a Villa Urbana.  The Villa was a scaled-up and more luxuriously "
"appointed version of the Domus.  A rich Roman would often try to spend "
"as much time at his\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#150Previous Page# / #152Next Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les villes de Province pouvaient comporter quelques Insulae, mais la "
"place n'était pas aussi vitale qu'à Rome, la plupart des citoyens "
"possédaient une Domus, même si elle était petite.\n"
"\n"
"Les Romains les plus riches pouvaient s'offrir le luxe d'une maison de "
"campagne, appelée Villa Urbana. La Villa était la version plus grande "
"et plus luxueuse de la Domus. Le riche Romain essayait d'y passer le "
"plus de temps\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#150Page Précédente# / #152Page Suivante#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/152/0"
msgid "Roman Housing (Cont.)"
msgstr "Habitat Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/152/1"
msgid ""
"Villa as possible, away from the noise, smell, and heat of city life.  \n"
"\n"
" The Emperor, of course, didn't have to settle for a Domus. He, his "
"family, and his huge staff all lived in the Imperial Palace on top of "
"the Palatine Hill.  The Palatine, believed by Romans to be the site "
"where Romulus founded their city, was reserved for the exclusive use of "
"the Emperor.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#151Previous Page#\n"
"#145Help# / #146Tips#"
msgstr ""
"possible, loin du bruit, des odeurs et de la chaleur de la vie urbaine.\n"
"\n"
"L'Empereur n'avait bien sûr pas à construire de maison. Il vivait "
"entouré de sa famille et son immense personnel dans le Palais Impérial "
"en haut du Mont Palatin. Les Romains pensaient que Romulus fonda leur "
"cité sur le Palatin qui était réservé à l'Empereur.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#151Page Précédente#\n"
"#145Aide# / #146Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/153/0"
msgid "The Centurion (page 5)"
msgstr "HUTTE"

msgctxt "help/153/1"
msgid ""
"proportion to the other Cohorts in the Legion. Under the Minor setting, "
"the Cohort will receive a slightly lower proportion of new recruits, "
"and under the Major setting, the Cohort will receive a slightly larger "
"proportion of new soldiers.\n"
"\n"
"A Cohort will perform better if its Morale is high. Morale will rise "
"after a Cohort is victorious in battle and will fall if it loses a "
"battle.\n"
"\n"
"If you Demobilize a Cohort, the Cohort will stop receiving new recruits "
"from the training pool.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#23Previous Page#\n"
"#13Tips#"
msgstr "Il n'y a aucune information sur ce sujet."

