msgctxt "help/280/0"
msgid "Help with Forums"
msgstr "Aide: Le Forum"

msgctxt "help/280/1"
msgid ""
"Forums are your city's centers of government. Their primary role is to "
"collect industrial taxes from your businesses and population taxes from "
"your citizens. They also act as gathering places for the masses, so "
"people will want to live near them. An absence of forum access will "
"limit a neighborhood's growth.\n"
"\n"
"Your forums must be adequately linked via roads to all houses and "
"businesses in the city. Forums send out Forum Clerks to visit housing "
"areas and bring in municipal cash.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#39Next Page#\n"
"#281Tips# / #282History#"
msgstr ""
"Les Forums sont les centres de gouvernement de la cité. Le premier rôle "
"est de collecter les taxes industrielles et individuelles auprès des "
"citoyens. Ce sont aussi des lieux de rassemblement populaires auprès "
"desquels les gens aiment vivre. L'absence d'accès aux Forums limite la "
"croissance du voisinage.\n"
"\n"
"Vos Forums doivent être reliés par des routes à toutes les maisons et "
"aux industries de la cité. Ils envoient des Commis du Forum visiter les "
"zones habitées et ramener des liquidités.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#39Page Suivante#\n"
"#281Trucs# / #282Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/281/0"
msgid "Tips for Forums"
msgstr "Trucs: Les Forums"

msgctxt "help/281/1"
msgid ""
"As a city grows you'll be able to build larger, more effective forums.  "
"You might want to leave room around the small forums you build, so that "
"you can improve them later.\n"
"\n"
"If your tax coverage seems to vary in part of your city, try adding a "
"forum to the area, or changing the road network there to include more "
"or fewer crossings. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#280Help# / #282History#"
msgstr ""
"Au cours de la croissance de votre cité, vous pouvez construire des "
"Forums plus grands et efficaces. Laissez de la place autour des petits "
"Forums afin de pouvoir les agrandir plus tard.\n"
"\n"
"Si la collecte des taxes semble varier à un endroit de la cité, essayez "
"d'ajouter un Forum ou de modifier le réseau routier pour ajouter ou "
"retirer des carrefours. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#280Aide# / #282Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/282/0"
msgid "The Roman Forum"
msgstr "Le Forum Romain"

msgctxt "help/282/1"
msgid ""
"The Forum of Augustus\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#283Next Page#\n"
"#280Help#/#281Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Le Forum d'Auguste\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#283Page Suivante#\n"
"#280Aide#/#281Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/283/0"
msgid "The Roman Forum"
msgstr "Le Forum Romain"

msgctxt "help/283/1"
msgid ""
"During the time of Rome's Etruscan kings (prior to 509 BC), the word "
"\"forum\" simply referred to the little marshy valley area between the "
"Capitoline and Palatine hills where the city dwellers would go to trade "
"goods, settle disputes, and gossip.  As time progressed, the valley was "
"drained and buildings dedicated to the political, judicial, and "
"administrative tasks of the settlement sprouted on the valley floor.  "
"The whole area was landscaped and remade into a place fit to become the "
"heart of the greatest city of the ancient world.  \n"
"\n"
" The forum was the social and political center of Rome.  Temples, "
"fountains, baths, and public \n"
"#282Previous Page#/#284Next Page#\n"
"#280Help#/#281Tips#"
msgstr ""
"A l'époque des rois Etrusques de Rome (antérieure à 509 avant JC), le "
"mot \"forum\" se rapportait juste à une petite vallée marécageuse située "
"entre les collines du Capitole et du Palatin où les habitants de la "
"cité faisaient du commerce, apaisaient les discordes ou bavardaient. Au "
"fil des temps, la vallée fut drainée et on y éleva des édifices dédiés "
"aux tâches politiques, judiciaires et administratives des colonies "
"implantées dans la vallée. Toute la zone fut ensuite nivelée et "
"reconstruite pour devenir le coeur de la plus grande Cité du monde "
"antique.\n"
"\n"
"Le Forum était le coeur social et politique de Rome. Les temples, les "
"fontaines, les bains et les lieux de loisirs\n"
"#282Page Précédente#/#284Page Suivante#\n"
"#280Aide#/#281Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/284/0"
msgid "The Roman Forum (cont.)"
msgstr "Le Forum Romain (suite)"

msgctxt "help/284/1"
msgid ""
"entertainment facilities surrounded it on every side.  Public debate on "
"important issues took place there, as did important trials.  The Roman "
"equivalent of the daily newspaper, the Acta Diurna, was posted on the "
"wall every day to be read or copied down by the eager citizens.  \n"
"\n"
" This original meeting place, the Forum Romanum Magnum, was sufficient "
"for the city's needs until  Imperial times.  When Julius Caesar claimed "
"dictatorship, one of his first acts was to build an entirely new forum, "
"the Forum of Caesar, in the same area, probably as a strong symbol of "
"the new political order.  The cost of building this forum was enormous, "
"since land within the original valley area was extremely scarce and "
"therefore expensive.  Later emperors copied Caesar's grandiose gesture, "
"until by \n"
"#283Previous Page#/#285Next Page#\n"
"#280Help#/#281Tips#"
msgstr ""
"publics l'entouraient. On y trouvait des débats publics sur des "
"problèmes importants, ainsi que de grands procès. L'équivalent Romain "
"du journal, l'Acta Diurna, était placardé sur les murs tous les jours "
"et les citoyens qui le désiraient pouvaient le lire ou le copier.\n"
"Ce lieu de rencontre original, le Forum Romanum Magnum, suffit aux "
"besoins de la Cité jusqu'à l'ère Impériale. Lorsque Jules César "
"proclama la dictature, un de ses premiers actes fut de construire un "
"forum totalement nouveau, le Forum de César, dans la même zone, un fort "
"symbole du nouvel ordre politique. Le coût de sa construction fut "
"énorme, la terre étant peu abondante et très chère à cet endroit. Plus "
"tard, les empereurs imitèrent le geste grandiose de César. Jusqu'à la "
"fin de\n"
"#283Page Précédente#/#285Page Suivante#\n"
"#280Aide#/#281Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/285/0"
msgid "The Roman Forum (cont.)"
msgstr "Le Forum Romain (suite)"

msgctxt "help/285/1"
msgid ""
"the end of the Empire there were six forums in the valley:  the "
"original and Caesar's, plus the Forum of Augustus, the Forum of "
"Vespasian, the forum of Nerva, and the Forum of Trajan. This last "
"forum, built between 112 and 114 AD, was the grandest of the lot, and "
"doubled the area occupied by the previous five forums. As a rule, new "
"forums were built just after times of serious political unrest -- which "
"was undoubtedly no coincidence. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#284Previous Page#\n"
"#280Help#/#281Tips#"
msgstr ""
"l'Empire, on dénombra six forums dans la vallée: l'originel et celui de "
"César auxquels vinrent s'ajouter ceux d'Auguste, de Vespasien, de Nerva "
"et de Trajan. Ce dernier, érigé entre les années 112 et 114 de notre "
"ère, était le plus grand de tous et avait le double de la taille de ses "
"prédécesseurs. Généralement, ils furent édifiés après des périodes de "
"sérieux troubles politiques -- ce qui n'était pas une coïncidence.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#284Page Précédente#\n"
"#280Aide#/#281Trucs#"

