msgctxt "help/328/0"
msgid "Roman Plazas"
msgstr "Les places"

msgctxt "help/328/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans built plazas in well-traveled public areas such as the Forum "
"Valley, and around important buildings such as major temples and the "
"Imperial palace.  Plazas were open areas paved with cut rock, sometimes "
"decorated with patterns of colored stone. Many of Rome's strictly "
"decorative monuments were located on plazas, particularly the victory "
"columns and arches earned by triumphant generals --  structures such as "
"the Column of Trajan, depicting the Emperor's conquest of the province "
"of Dacia, and the Arch of Septimius Severus, commemorating his "
"victories over the Parthians, Arabs, and Mesopotamians. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#327Previous Page#\n"
"#325Help#/#326Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les Romains construisaient des Places dans les zones fréquentées, comme "
"la Vallée du Forum, et près d'édifices importants comme les temples "
"majeurs ou le Palais Impérial. Les places sont des zones pavées "
"ouvertes, parfois décorées de motifs de pierre colorée. On y trouvait "
"la plupart des monuments Romains à but uniquement décoratif, en "
"particulier les colonnes et arcs de triomphe des généraux -- structures "
"telles que la Colonne de Trajan, retraçant la conquête de la Province "
"de Dacie, et l'arche de Septime Sévère célébrant sa victoire sur les "
"Parthes, les Arabes et les peuples de Mésopotamie.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#327Page Précédente#\n"
"#325Aide#/#326Trucs#"

