msgctxt "help/340/0"
msgid "Aqueducts"
msgstr "Les Réservoirs et Aqueducs"

msgctxt "help/340/1"
msgid ""
"You may place a length of aqueduct by clicking on a line of map "
"squares, one at a time, or by dragging across a map area while holding "
"your mouse button down. An aqueduct can only be used to send water from "
"one reservoir to another reservoir. In this way, you can send water all "
"over your city. You cannot connect aqueducts to Fountains or Wells.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#341Tips# / #342History#"
msgstr ""
"La longueur d'un aqueduc n'affecte pas ses performances -- seul le "
"nombre de réservoirs alimentés le peut. Cependant, l'entretient de "
"longs aqueducs nécessite une forte main d'oeuvres de Plébéiens. "
"Plusieurs aqueducs peuvent partir du même réservoir et créer un \"arbre\" "
"dont les branches atteignent plusieurs zones de la cité.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#341Trucs# / #342Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/341/0"
msgid "Tips for Reservoirs and Aqueducts"
msgstr "Trucs: Les Réservoirs et Aqueducs"

msgctxt "help/341/1"
msgid ""
"The length of an aqueduct does not affect its performance -- only the "
"number of reservoirs supplied by it does.  However, longer aqueducts "
"require more plebeian maintenance. You can run several aqueducts off of "
"the same reservoir, to create a \"water tree\" that has branches in "
"different parts of the city. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#340Help# / #342History#"
msgstr ""
"La longueur d'un aqueduc n'affecte pas ses performances -- seul le "
"nombre de réservoirs alimentés le peut. Cependant, l'entretient de "
"longs aqueducs nécessite une forte main d'oeuvres de Plébéiens. "
"Plusieurs aqueducs peuvent partir du même réservoir et créer un \"arbre\" "
"dont les branches atteignent plusieurs zones de la cité. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#340Aide# / #342Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/342/0"
msgid "Roman Aqueducts"
msgstr "Les Aqueducs"

msgctxt "help/342/1"
msgid ""
"The aqueduct system that brought plentiful fresh water to Rome's "
"denizens was an engineering marvel.  The first one, the Aqua Appia, was "
"built in 312 BC by Appius Claudius Caecus, the same man who built the "
"Appian Way, Rome's first major road.  It carried water into the city "
"from a spring ten miles to the east, running underground for most of "
"its length. As it neared the city, it was elevated onto the famous "
"Roman aqueduct arches, so that water could be piped into the wealthy "
"hilltop dwellings.  \n"
"\n"
" At its height, Rome had at least fourteen separate aqueducts, which "
"spanned 316 miles and brought in 60 million cubic feet of fresh water "
"each day.  The \n"
"#343Next Page#\n"
"#340Help#/#341Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Le système d'aqueducs qui alimenta les citoyens Romains en eau fraîche "
"était une pure merveille d'ingéniosité. Le premier, l'Aqua Appia, fut "
"bâti en 312 avant JC par Appius Claudius Caecus, le même qui "
"construisit la Via Appia, la première grande route de Rome. Il amenait "
"à la ville l'eau d'une source située à une quinzaine de kilomètres à "
"l'est. Souterrain sur la majeure partie de son trajet, il s'élevait à "
"l'approche de la Cité sur les fameuses arches des aqueducs Romains afin "
"que l'eau puisse être pompée pour les riches demeures situées sur les "
"collines.\n"
"A son apogée, Rome était alimentée par au moins quatorze aqueducs "
"séparés qui s'étendaient sur 508 kilomètres et amenaient 180 000 mètres "
"cubes d'eau par jour.\n"
"#343Page Suivante#\n"
"#340Aide#/#341Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/343/0"
msgid "Roman Aqueducts (cont.)"
msgstr "Les Aqueducs Romains (suite)"

msgctxt "help/343/1"
msgid ""
"longest city aqueduct was the Aqua Marcia which extended more than 56 "
"miles.  This extensive system wasn't restricted to Rome proper; any "
"major Roman city had a similar arrangement.  The aqueduct system at "
"what would become modern day Lyons was equivalent to Rome's in every "
"way.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#342Previous Page#\n"
"#340Help#/#341Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Le plus long aqueduc de la Cité était le Aqua Marcia d'une longueur de "
"90 kilomètres. Ce système n'était pas réservé à la seule Rome, toute "
"cité Romaine importante disposait d'un tel équipement. Le système "
"d'aqueducs de l'actuelle ville de Lyon était en tout point similaire.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#342Page Précédente#\n"
"#340Aide#/#341Trucs#"

