msgctxt "help/385/0"
msgid "Fountains"
msgstr "Les Fontaines"

msgctxt "help/385/1"
msgid ""
"Fountains create the largest area of water supply. A fountain must be "
"placed within a reservoir's zone of pipe access. It will then use the "
"pipe access to create a usable water supply for the area around it. "
"Multiple fountains can draw from a single reservoir. Building a network "
"of fountains supplied by reservoirs is a very effective way of "
"supplying your city with water.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#386Tips# / #387History#"
msgstr ""
"La fontaine crée la plus grande zone de distribution de l'eau. Elle "
"doit être placée dans le rayon d'accès des tuyaux du réservoir. Elle "
"utilisera alors ces tuyaux pour devenir le point d'eau potable des "
"environs. Plusieurs fontaines peuvent puiser dans un même réservoir. La "
"création d'un réseau de fontaines alimentées par les réservoirs et la "
"meilleure façon de distribuer l'eau dans la ville.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#386Trucs# / #387Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/386/0"
msgid "Tips for Fountains"
msgstr "Trucs : fontaines"

msgctxt "help/386/1"
msgid ""
"By building fountains at the farthest corners of a reservoir's area of "
"pipe access, you can cover a large square area with water supply.  "
"However, this doesn't mean that these are the most convenient locations "
"for fountains in your city. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#385Help# / #387History#"
msgstr ""
"En plaçant une fontaine au point le plus éloigné de l'accès des tuyaux "
"d'un réservoir, vous pouvez alimenter une grande zone en eau. Cela ne "
"signifie cependant pas que ce sont les meilleurs emplacement pour les "
"fontaines de votre cité. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#385Aide# / #387Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/387/0"
msgid "The Fountains of Rome"
msgstr "Les Fontaines de Rome"

msgctxt "help/387/1"
msgid ""
"The Trevi Fountain\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Next Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"La fontaine Trevi\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Page Suivante#\n"
"#385Aide#/#386Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/388/0"
msgid "Fountains"
msgstr "Les Fontaines"

msgctxt "help/388/1"
msgid ""
"From ancient times to the present, Rome has been famous for its "
"magnificent fountains.  Numerous songs and stories have been inspired "
"by their constant flow.  In ancient Rome, the fountains served a double "
"purpose  as sources of fresh water for the public and as works of art.  "
"The fountains were linked to reservoirs by a pipe network usually made "
"of ceramic, though the much more expensive lead was infrequently used.  "
"Carved wooden pipes also sometimes made an appearance.   \n"
"\n"
"The oldest fountain in Rome is a natural spring, the Lacus Juturnae in "
"the Forum valley.  New fountains were built as they were needed, or as "
"they were \n"
"#387Previous Page#/#389Next Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"De l'Antiquité à nos jours, Rome a été fameuse pour ses magnifiques "
"fontaines. Leur débit constant a inspiré bien des chansons et des "
"histoires. Dans la Rome antique, leur vocation était double: source "
"d'eau fraîche publique et ouvrage d'art. Les fontaines étaient reliées "
"aux réservoirs par un réseau de tuyaux, généralement en céramique, bien "
"que des matériaux plus chers étaient parfois employés. On voyait "
"parfois des tuyaux de bois sculpté.\n"
" La plus vielle fontaine de Rome est une source naturelle, la Lacus "
"Juturnae située dans la vallée du Forum. Les nouvelles fontaines "
"étaient construites là ou elles étaient nécessaires, ou là ou on les "
"demandait\n"
"#387Page Précédente#/#389Page Suivante#\n"
"#385Aide#/#386Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/389/0"
msgid "The Fountains of Rome (cont.)"
msgstr "Les Fontaines de Rome (suite)"

msgctxt "help/389/1"
msgid ""
"wanted -- fountains were often used as monuments to famous people or "
"events.  As of 270 AD, Rome had more than 1,200 public fountains.  \n"
"\n"
"One of the most famous fountains in Rome is the Trevi fountain, "
"originally constructed during ancient times but completely remodeled "
"and rebuilt in recent centuries.  This fountain, like many of Rome's "
"fountains, has a legend associated with it that says anyone who throws "
"a coin in the fountain is guaranteed a return to Rome.  Its waters come "
"from the Aqua Vergine, and have been considered the city's best-tasting "
"for centuries.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Previous Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"-- les fontaines servaient souvent de monuments en mémoire de "
"personnages ou d'événements. Vers 270 après JC, Rome disposait de plus "
"de 1200 fontaines publiques.\n"
"\n"
"L'une des plus fameuses fontaines de Rome est la Fontaine Trevi, "
"construite dans l'Antiquité mais totalement remodelée et reconstruite "
"au cours des derniers siècles. Une légende est associée à cette "
"fontaine, comme à bien d'autres à Rome. Elle dit que quiconque y jette "
"une pièce de monnaie est assuré de revenir à Rome. Son eau vient de "
"l'Aqua Vergine et a toujours été considérée comme la meilleure de la "
"cité.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Page Précédente#\n"
"#385Aide#/#386Trucs#"

