msgctxt "help/460/0"
msgid "Praefectures"
msgstr "Les Préfectures"

msgctxt "help/460/1"
msgid ""
"Praefectures send out vigiles, or watchmen, who patrol the city in "
"search of rioters and fires. A strong vigile presence will help prevent "
"riots before they start (fires may be prevented by assigning Plebs to "
"fire duty). If a fire or a riot does break out, the vigiles will take "
"care of it automatically as soon as they discover the problem. Like "
"soldiers, vigiles will enhance the security of any area they walk past. "
"Like Barracks, Praefectures are undesirable to live near, so they limit "
"land value. Make sure that there is good road access between your "
"praefectures and your housing.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#461Tips# / #462History#"
msgstr ""
"Les préfectures envoient des Vigiles, ou surveillants, patrouiller dans "
"la cité en quête d'émeutiers ou de feux. Une forte présence de vigiles "
"empêche les émeutes d'éclater (les incendies peuvent être évités en "
"assignant des Plébéiens à leur surveillance). Si un incendie ou une "
"émeute éclate, les vigiles s'en occupent dès qu'ils découvrent le "
"problème. Comme les soldats, les vigiles augmente la sécurité dans les "
"zones qu'ils traversent. Comme les Casernes, les Préfectures ne sont "
"pas des endroits près desquels il fait bon vivre, aussi elles limitent "
"le coût foncier. Veillez à installer un bon accès routier entre les "
"Préfectures et les maisons.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#461Trucs# / #462Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/461/0"
msgid "Tips for Praefectures"
msgstr "Trucs: Les Préfectures"

msgctxt "help/461/1"
msgid ""
"Prafectures are small.  Building more than one of them along a single "
"road can improve their coverage of an area. If a fire has already "
"broken out, and you did not prepare for it by building praefectures, an "
"expensive solution is to build a group of them near the fire.  Make "
"sure that the praefectures are next to roads -- or else they can't send "
"out vigiles -- and make sure they aren't so close to the fire that they "
"catch fire themselves! \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#460Help# / #462History#"
msgstr ""
"Les préfectures sont petites. En bâtir plusieurs le long d'une seule "
"route peut améliorer leur zone de couverture. Si un incendie a déjà "
"éclaté et que vous n'avez pas encore de préfecture, il existe une "
"solution coûteuse qui consiste à en construire un groupe près de "
"l'incendie. Veillez à construire les préfectures près des routes -- "
"sinon elle ne pourraient pas envoyer de vigiles -- et ne les approchez "
"pas trop de l'incendie car elles pourraient elles-mêmes s'enflammer ! \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#460Aide# / #462Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/462/0"
msgid "Praefectures"
msgstr "Les Préfectures"

msgctxt "help/462/1"
msgid ""
"The threat of fire was easily the greatest danger to the citizens of "
"Rome. Although the insulae had stone bases, the upper floors were "
"mostly timber. Since all lighting, heating, and cooking came from open "
"flames, fires were common and inevitable. Once ignited, a fire could "
"easily jump the narrow streets and the gaps between insulae, to spread "
"unchecked throughout the city. \n"
"\n"
" Until the reign of the Emperor Augustus, Rome had nothing resembling a "
"fire department. The wealthy and unscrupulous Roman general, Marcus "
"Licinius Crassus, organized a private corps of men trained to fight "
"fires during the last years of the Republic, but \n"
"#463Next Page#\n"
"#460Help#/#461Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les incendies constituaient sans aucun doute la plus grande menace pour "
"les citoyens Romains. Bien que la base des Insulae fût en pierre, les "
"étages supérieurs étaient principalement en bois. L'éclairage, le "
"chauffage et la cuisine émanant de flammes vives, les incendies étaient "
"courants et inévitables. Après l'embrasement, un incendie pouvait "
"aisément traverser les ruelles étroites et les espaces entre Insulae "
"pour se répandre dans la ville.\n"
"Jusqu'au règne de l'Empereur Auguste, Rome n'eût rien qui ressemblait à "
"des pompiers. Le riche et peu scrupuleux général Romain Marcus Licinius "
"Crassus, organisa un corps privé composé d'hommes entraînés à combattre "
"le feu au cours des dernières années de la République, mais\n"
"#463Page Suivante#\n"
"#460Aide#/#461Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/463/0"
msgid "Praefectures"
msgstr "Les Préfectures"

msgctxt "help/463/1"
msgid ""
"they were not precisely public servants. When a fire broke out, Crassus "
"would accompany his men to the scene and make the distraught owner an "
"outrageously low offer for the burning building. If the owner accepted, "
"Crassus' men would extinguish the fire; if not, the building would be "
"allowed to burn to the ground.\n"
"\n"
" Julius Caesar tried to do something about the problem by decreeing "
"that all buildings had to be roofed with non-flammable tiles, and that "
"they had to be built at least three feet apart.  But it fell to his "
"successor, Augustus, to organize an official fire brigade for the city, "
"paid for from state funds. Augustus' workers, known as vigiles, were "
"stationed in buildings called praefectures.  In addition to answering "
"fire alarms, they also served as night watchmen in general, at \n"
"#462Previous Page#/#464Next Page#\n"
"#460Help#/#461Tips#"
msgstr ""
"ce n'était pas vraiment un service public. Quand un incendie éclatait, "
"Crassus accompagnait ses hommes sur les lieux du sinistre et faisait au "
"propriétaire affolé une offre outrageusement basse pour l'immeuble en "
"feu. S'il acceptait, les hommes de Crassus éteignaient le feu; sinon, "
"il brûlait jusqu'à terre.\n"
"\n"
"Jules César tenta de lutter contre ce problème en décrétant que tous "
"les immeubles devaient être couverts de tuiles ininflammables et qu'ils "
"devaient être séparés d'au moins un mètre. Mais il échut à son "
"successeur, Auguste, d'organiser un corps officiel de pompiers pour la "
"Cité, payé par les fonds publics. Ces hommes, connus sous le nom de "
"Vigiles, stationnaient dans des immeubles appelés Préfectures. En plus "
"de combattre les incendies, ils servaient également de veilleurs de "
"nuit,\n"
"#462Page Précédente#/#464Page Suivante#\n"
"#460Aide#/#461Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/464/0"
msgid "Praefectures"
msgstr "Les Préfectures"

msgctxt "help/464/1"
msgid ""
"least for the better neighborhoods. There were seven squads of vigiles, "
"each with 1,000 men. Despite their vital function, the were held in low "
"esteem by many citizens, who called them \"Bucketmen.\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#463Previous Page#\n"
"#460Help#/#461Tips#"
msgstr ""
"au moins pour le voisinage immédiat. Il y avait sept escouades de "
"vigiles, comportant chacune 1000 hommes. Malgré leur fonction "
"essentielle, ils étaient peu estimés par de nombreux citoyens qui les "
"appelaient les \"porteurs de seau\".\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#463Page Précédente#\n"
"#460Aide#/#461Trucs#"

