msgctxt "help/550/0"
msgid "Help with Circuses"
msgstr "Aide : les Cirques"

msgctxt "help/550/1"
msgid ""
"The circus is an oblong track where chariot races are held. The larger "
"Circus Maximus is an impressive building that will draw huge crowds and "
"impact a larger region. Circuses are rectangular in shape.\n"
"\n"
"You may place one in any orientation in your city by using the rotate "
"arrows on your control panel.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#551Tips# / #552History#"
msgstr ""
"Un cirque est une piste oblongue pour les courses de chars. Le grand "
"Cirque Maxime est un édifice impressionnant qui attire des foules "
"importantes et touche une grande région. Les cirques sont de forme "
"rectangulaire.\n"
"\n"
"Vous pouvez en placer un dans toute orientation avec les flèches de "
"rotation du panneau de contrôle.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#551Trucs# / #552Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/551/0"
msgid "Tips for Entertainment "
msgstr "Trucs: les Cirques"

msgctxt "help/551/1"
msgid ""
"When you have access to improved entertainment, you should consider "
"\"upgrading\" the ones you have already built.  You can easily replace "
"your old ones with odeums and coliseums, as they take up the same "
"space.  On the other hand, the Circus Maximus is larger than the "
"Circus, so you plan to clear extra space for it.\n"
"\n"
"If you can't afford to build the more expensive forms of entertainment, "
"you should still prepare space for them in your city.  For example, if "
"you try to arrange as many city blocks around a clearing that will "
"eventually hold a circus, than you won't need to build so many "
"circuses. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#550Help# / #552History#"
msgstr ""
"Lorsque vous avez accès à une meilleure catégorie de loisirs, vous "
"devez envisager d'améliorer ceux qui existent déjà. Vous pouvez "
"aisément remplacer les anciens par des Odéons et des Colisées qui "
"occupent le même espace. D'un autre point de vue, le Cirque Maxime est "
"plus grand que le Cirque, vous devez donc lui libérer de la place.\n"
"\n"
"Si vous ne pouvez pas vous permettre de construire les formes de "
"loisirs les plus coûteuses, vous pouvez leur préparer un espace dans la "
"cité. Par exemple, si vous essayez d'agencer autant d'îlots que "
"possible autour d'un espace qui pourrait contenir un cirque, vous "
"n'aurez pas à construire autant de cirques. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#550Aide# / #552Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/552/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus"
msgstr "Le Cirque Romain"

msgctxt "help/552/1"
msgid ""
"The prescription of the writer Juvenal for a happy citizenry came down "
"to two essentials: \"Bread and Circuses.\"  Juvenal undoubtedly selected "
"circuses because the chariot races held in these buildings were the "
"most popular spectator sport in the city of Rome.  Charioteers were "
"organized into teams by color -- the Greens, the Blues, the Reds, and "
"the Whites -- and their standings were hotly contested and wagered on. "
"Successful chariot drivers had fan clubs who followed their careers.\n"
"\n"
"At its height, Rome had a total of four circuses. The undisputed king "
"of these was the Circus Maximus, located in the valley between the "
"Palatine and \n"
"#553Next Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""
"L'écrivain Juvénal disait que pour rendre les citoyens heureux il "
"fallait leur donner \"du pain et des jeux\". Juvénal choisit sans doute "
"les cirques car on y tenait le sport le plus spectaculaire et populaire "
"de Rome: les courses de chars. Les chars étaient organisés en équipes "
"de couleurs -- les Verts, les Bleus, les Rouges et les Blancs -- la "
"concurrence et les paris étaient importants. Les meilleurs conducteurs "
"avaient des 'fan-club'. qui suivaient leur carrière.\n"
"\n"
"A son apogée, Rome disposait de quatre cirques. Le roi incontesté était "
"le Cirque Maxime, situé dans la vallée entre les collines du Palatin et\n"
"#553Page Suivante#\n"
"#550Aide#/#551Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/553/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus (Cont.)"
msgstr "Le Cirque Romain (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/553/1"
msgid ""
"Aventine hills. It was essentially complete as early as 329 BC, "
"although it was modified and added onto as time went by.  This huge "
"structure measured 654 by 218 yards, roughly the size of a dozen or so "
"football fields laid side by side. It could seat somewhere between "
"255,000 and 385,000 racing enthusiasts at a time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#552Previous Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""
"de l'Aventin. Il fut terminé pour l'essentiel en 329 avant JC, bien "
"qu'il fut modifié et agrandi au fil du temps. Cette immense structure "
"mesurait 600 x 200 mètres, la taille d'une douzaine de stades de "
"football côte à côte. il pouvait contenir entre 255 000 et 385 000 "
"spectateurs enthousiastes.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#552Page Précédente#\n"
"#550Aide#/#551Trucs#"

