msgctxt "help/625/0"
msgid "Help with Businesses"
msgstr "Aide: Industries"

msgctxt "help/625/1"
msgid ""
"Businesses take raw materials from outside the city and use them to "
"produce consumer goods A winery, for example, will use grapes to make "
"wine. A business will transport its processed wares to a market to be "
"sold.\n"
"\n"
"Like markets, businesses limit housing development. They do need a "
"local work force, however, so you may have to build some housing "
"nearby. Walking workers near your businesses will represent the work "
"force. Businesses will look for workers nearby in a square radius.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1072Previous Page# / #41Next Page#\n"
"#626Tips# "
msgstr ""
"Les industries prennent des matières premières en dehors de la cité et "
"les utilisent pour produire des biens de consommation. Par exemple, un "
"vigneron utilise des grappes de raisin pour faire du vin. Les produits "
"finis sont ensuite transportés au marché pour y être vendus.\n"
"\n"
"Comme les marchés, les industries limitent le développement de "
"l'habitat. Il leur faut des travailleurs locaux, vous aurez donc à "
"construire quelques maisons dans leur voisinage. Les travailleurs "
"marchant près de vos industries représentent les effectifs. Les "
"industries recherchent les travailleurs dans le carré immédiat.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1072Page Précédente# / #41Page Suivante#\n"
"#626Trucs# "

msgctxt "help/626/0"
msgid "Tips for Businesses"
msgstr "Trucs: les industries"

msgctxt "help/626/1"
msgid ""
"You can employ several businesses with the same block of housing, if "
"you build them on all sides of the block.  However, the houses will be "
"limited by low land value. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#625Help# "
msgstr ""
"Le même bloc de maisons peut servir plusieurs industries, il suffit de "
"les construire tout autour de celui-ci. Cependant le coût foncier se "
"trouve limité. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#625Aide# "

