msgctxt "help/655/0"
msgid "Help with Markets"
msgstr "Aide: Marchés"

msgctxt "help/655/1"
msgid ""
"Markets allow commerce to take place in your city. Markets send out "
"traders who use the city's road system to seek out potential customers. "
"In addition to the general business they do, markets will also sell the "
"goods produced by businesses in the city. Markets will have little "
"colored awnings that represent their trade. The busier the market, the "
"more awnings you will see around it, so its performance is apparent at "
"a glance.\n"
"\n"
"To succeed, markets need good road access, and a steady supply of goods "
"from city businesses. Although residents need access, they do not like "
"being too close to markets -- this tends to limit land values. \n"
"\n"
"#656Tips# / #657History#"
msgstr ""
"Les marchés permettent de mettre en place le commerce dans votre ville. "
"Ils envoient des marchands qui utilisent le système routier de la Cité "
"pour chercher des clients potentiels. En plus des affaires en général, "
"les marchés servent à vendre les produits de vos industries. Les "
"marchés ont un petit store coloré représentant leurs transactions. plus "
"il est actif, plus vous verrez de stores autour de lui, ses "
"performances sont donc immédiatement visibles.\n"
"\n"
"Pour être prospères, il leur faut un bon accès routier et un "
"approvisionnement stable en marchandises locales. Bien que les "
"résidents doivent y accéder, ils n'aime pas en être trop près, les "
"marchés limitant le coût foncier. \n"
"\n"
"#656Trucs# / #657Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/656/0"
msgid "Tips for Markets"
msgstr "Trucs: Marchés"

msgctxt "help/656/1"
msgid ""
"Markets will limit nearby land values, but not nearly as low as a "
"business or barracks.  If you are only trying to build \"middle-class\" "
"housing, don't worry about where you put your markets. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#655Help# / #657History#"
msgstr ""
"Les marchés limitent le coût foncier, mais pas autant que les "
"industries et les casernes. Si vous voulez vous contenter d'habitants "
"de \"classe moyenne\", l'emplacement des marchés n'a pas d'importance. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#655Aide# / #657Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/657/0"
msgid "Industry in Rome"
msgstr "L'industrie à Rome"

msgctxt "help/657/1"
msgid ""
"The city of Rome itself had little or no real industry.  Its wealth "
"sprang more from its central location in Italy (which made it a natural "
"center for trade), and from its position as the administrative capital "
"of the Empire than from any goods it could produce. The only real "
"industry in Rome centered around the necessity of providing food for "
"Rome's one million consumers. The rest of Rome's industry consisted of "
"thousands of small shopkeepers and artisans, usually operating out of "
"the first floor of some insula.  \n"
"\n"
"Rome had many specialized wholesale markets which sold only a single "
"commodity, and each had its own name. The holitorium sold vegetables, "
"the boarium \n"
"#658Next Page#\n"
"#655Help#/#656Tips#"
msgstr ""
"L'industrie à Rome même était presque inexistante. Sa richesse "
"provenait plus de sa position centrale en Italie (ce qui en fit un "
"centre d'échanges naturel), et de sa position en tant que capitale "
"administrative de l'Empire, que des richesses qu'elle pouvait produire. "
"La seule vraie industrie Romaine tenait dans le souci de nourrir un "
"million de consommateurs. Le reste de l'industrie romaine se résumait "
"en milliers de petits commerces et artisans, travaillant la plupart du "
"temps au premier étage d'une Insula.\n"
"\n"
"Rome possédait de nombreux marchés spécialisés vendant un seul type de "
"bien, chacun avait son propre nom.. L'holitorium vendait des légumes, "
"le boarium\n"
"#658Page Suivante#\n"
"#655Aide#/#656Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/658/0"
msgid "Industry in Rome (cont.)"
msgstr "L'industrie à Rome (suite)"

msgctxt "help/658/1"
msgid ""
"sold cattle, the suarium sold pigs, the vinarium sold wine, and so on. "
"There were also numerous general-purpose markets, usually permanent "
"buildings covered to keep the foodstuffs from spoiling quickly in the "
"direct sunlight. These markets could become quite grand -- Trajan's "
"Market featured three tiers of shops and a great covered market hall, "
"surely a close cousin to the modern-day shopping mall. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#657Previous Page#\n"
"#655Help#/#656Tips#"
msgstr ""
"du bétail, le suarium des cochons, le vinarium du vin et ainsi de "
"suite. Il y avait également de nombreux marchés généralistes, édifices "
"permanents et couverts qui évitaient à l'alimentation de se désagréger "
"rapidement à la lumière du soleil. Ces marchés pouvaient devenir "
"magnifiques -- le Marché de Trajan se composait de trois niveaux de "
"boutiques et d'un grand hall de marché couvert, un proche parent des "
"centres commerciaux actuels.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#657Page Précédente#\n"
"#655Aide#/#656Trucs#"

