msgctxt "help/805/0"
msgid "Border Towns"
msgstr "Villes frontières"

msgctxt "help/805/1"
msgid ""
"Border Towns have a special significance to your extra-provincial "
"trade. From them, you may receive goods from beyond your Province's "
"borders in the direction of the border town. To receive such goods, you "
"will need to build a Trading Post near the border town, and link it by "
"road to your Capital City. The closer the Trading Post is to a Border "
"Town, the easier it will be for the town to send you its trade goods.\n"
"\n"
"To see which goods any particular border town might supply, check with "
"the Merchant in your Forum. Any item listed with an overland trade "
"symbol and the name of a foreign province is an item that is availble "
"from the Border Town on the foreign province's side of your Province.  "
msgstr ""
"Ces villes ont une signification spéciale dans le commerce "
"inter-provinces. Elles permettent la réception de marchandises "
"provenant d'au-delà des frontières. Pour recevoir ces marchandises, "
"vous devez construire un Comptoir près de la Ville-frontière et le "
"relier par une route à la capitale. Plus un Comptoir est près d'une "
"ville-frontière, plus elle pourra envoyer ses marchandises rapidement.\n"
"\n"
"Pour savoir quelles marchandises vous pouvez trouver sur une frontière, "
"vérifiez avec le Marchand dans votre Forum. Tous les articles signalés "
"par un symbole \"caravane\" et le nom d'une Province étrangère sont "
"disponibles via la ville-frontière voisine de cette Province."

