msgctxt "help/835/0"
msgid "Help with Provincial Roads"
msgstr "Aide : Voies Romaines"

msgctxt "help/835/1"
msgid ""
"You may build highways on the Province Level the same way you build "
"roads on the City Level: simply click on the Roads icon, and place or "
"drag road sections square-by-square.\n"
"\n"
" There are no \"walkers\" on the Province Level, but it is vital that "
"most buildings you build be connected to your capital city via roads. A "
"good road system will do wonders to bring your Province together. When "
"you connect your city to small, isolated villages, you will most likely "
"see them grow and develop as they enhance your city's trade economy.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#839Next Page#\n"
"#836Tips# / #837History#"
msgstr ""
"Pour construire des voies en Mode Campagne procédez de la même façon "
"que pour construire des routes au Niveau Local: cliquez sur l'icône "
"Routes et placez ou glissez la souris case par case.\n"
"\n"
"Il n'y a pas de \"marcheurs\" en Mode Campagne, mais il est vital que les "
"édifices soient reliés à la capitale par une route. Un bon réseau "
"routier unifiera votre Province à merveille. Lorsque vous reliez votre "
"ville à des petits villages isolés, vous les voyez se développer et ils "
"améliorent les résultats commerciaux de la Cité.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#839Page Suivante#\n"
"#836Trucs# / #837Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/836/0"
msgid "Tips for Prov. Roads"
msgstr "Routes de Province"

msgctxt "help/836/1"
msgid ""
"When money is tight, try to build as few road connections between "
"industries as possible.  When you have more Denarii, you can consider "
"building roads solely for troop movement; but remember that your "
"enemies can use them as well.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#835Help# / #837History#"
msgstr ""
"Quand vous manquez d'argent, essayez de construire le moins possible de "
"connexions routières entre industries. Lorsque vous avez des Deniers, "
"vous pouvez envisager des routes qui ne serviront qu'aux troupes, en "
"n'oubliant pas que l'ennemi peut aussi les utiliser.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#835Aide# / #837Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/837/0"
msgid "Roman Highways"
msgstr "Voies"

msgctxt "help/837/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans were great road-builders. In many ways, their roads  were "
"the foundation of their Empire. They allowed easy movement of troops "
"for conquest, and of settlers and traders for gentler means of "
"Romanization. The speed at which people could travel over Roman "
"highways was not equaled until the era of the automobile. \n"
"\n"
" A Roman highway was between three and twelve yards wide.  To construct "
"it, a ditch was dug, which was then filled with several layers of "
"compressed gravel and chalk, then surfaced with brick or pebble "
"pavement. This work was done either by slave gangs or by the Roman "
"soldiers themselves.  The road \n"
"#838Next Page#\n"
"#835Help#/#836Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les Romains étaient de grands bâtisseurs de routes qui, par beaucoup de "
"points, étaient le fondement de leur Empire. Elles permettaient les "
"mouvements de troupes pour les conquêtes, de colons et de marchands, "
"pour les \"romanisations\" plus douces. La vitesse de déplacement sur ces "
"routes ne fût pas égalée avant l'ère de l'automobile.\n"
"\n"
"Une VOIE ROMAINE était large de deux à trois mètres. Pour les "
"construire, on creusait un fossé qui était ensuite comblé avec "
"plusieurs couches de gravats compressés et de calcaire; on les pavait "
"ensuite de briques ou de galets. Ce travail était accompli soit par des "
"esclaves, soit par les soldats romains eux-mêmes.\n"
"#838Page Suivante#\n"
"#835Aide#/#836Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/838/0"
msgid "Roman Highways (cont.)"
msgstr "Les Voies Romaines (suite)"

msgctxt "help/838/1"
msgid ""
"network of the Roman Empire streched for more than 87,000 miles at its "
"greatest extent, and the remains of these highways -- some even usable "
"-- can still be found in many places in Europe. \n"
"\n"
"In addition to soldiers and merchants, the provincial roads were useful "
"to tourists -- of whom there were many -- and to the official Post "
"Riders of Rome's reliable postal service. The highways featured "
"official state inns for government travelers on state business, as well "
"as private hostels for non-official travelers.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#837Previous Page#\n"
"#835Help#/#836Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Le réseau routier de l'Empire Romain s'étirait sur plus de 140 000 "
"kilomètres à son apogée, et il reste des voies romaines -- dont "
"certaines sont praticables -- partout en Europe. \n"
"Les voies étaient utiles non seulement aux soldats et aux marchands, "
"mais aussi aux touristes -- qui étaient nombreux -- et aux courriers "
"officiels de l'efficace service postal de Rome. Les voies romaines "
"proposaient des auberges d'état aux voyageurs gouvernementaux ou aux "
"commis de l'état, et des hostelleries privées aux particuliers.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#837Page Précédente#\n"
"#835Aide#/#836Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/839/0"
msgid "Provinical Roads (cont.)"
msgstr "Les Voies Romaines (suite)"

msgctxt "help/839/1"
msgid ""
"On the down side, roads also allow invading Barbarians to travel "
"faster. You may build roads through Grasslands and Woodlands, but not "
"through Mountain Ranges, Farm or Quarry/Mine Land, or on top of Towns.\n"
"\n"
"Commerce will pass through towns and other structures, but Cohorts will "
"not.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#835Previous Page#\n"
"#836Tips# / #837History#"
msgstr ""
"Par contre, les routes permettent aussi aux barbares de voyager "
"rapidement. Vous pouvez construire des routes à travers les prairies et "
"les forêts mais pas dans les montagnes, les fermes, carrières, mines ni "
"sur les villes. \n"
"\n"
"Le commerce passe par les villes et autres structures mais les cohortes "
"ne le peuvent pas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#835Page Précédente#\n"
"#836Trucs# / #837Histoire#"

