msgctxt "help/865/0"
msgid "Provincial Walls"
msgstr "Les murs"

msgctxt "help/865/1"
msgid ""
"Provincial Wall construction works in the same way as City Wall "
"construction on the City Level. You may enclose all of your Province's "
"exposed borders, or you may enclose only part of your Province.\n"
"\n"
"But be aware: if you separate economic sources (Farms, Quarries, etc.) "
"or towns from your city, their output will be diminished. All sources "
"within your Province want to be protected, so you should avoid dividing "
"your province.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#866Tips# / #867History#"
msgstr ""
"Les murs construits en Province fonctionnent de la même façon que ceux "
"construits au niveau local. Vous pouvez entourer la totalité des "
"frontières exposées de votre Province, ou seulement une partie de la "
"Province.\n"
"\n"
"Mais soyez prudent: si vous séparez les sources économiques (Fermes, "
"Carrières, etc.) ou les villes de votre Cité, leurs envois "
"s'amenuisent. Vous devez protéger toutes les sources de votre Province, "
"aussi évitez de la diviser.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#866Trucs# / #867Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/866/0"
msgid "Tips for Provincial Walls"
msgstr "Trucs : murs des provinces"

msgctxt "help/866/1"
msgid ""
"If you think that you can complete a province without using certain "
"distant meadows or rocky areas, then feel free to leave them outside of "
"your provincial walls.\n"
"\n"
"Use mountains as natural barriers to save on the cost of provincial "
"walls.  Build walls across valleys which enemies tend to approach from. "
" Also build gates in provincial walls, to that cohorts can get to "
"either side of the wall as needed.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#865Help# / #867History#"
msgstr ""
"Si vous pensez pouvoir réaliser votre Province sans utiliser des zones "
"rocailleuses ou des prés éloignés, vous pouvez les laisser hors des "
"murs provinciaux.\n"
"\n"
"Utilisez les montagnes comme barrières naturelles pour réduire le coût "
"des murs. Construisez des murs à travers les vallées menacées par "
"l'ennemi. Pensez à ajouter des portails dans les murs pour que vos "
"cohortes puissent accéder à volonté aux deux côtés du mur.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#865Aide# / #867Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/867/0"
msgid "Provincial Walls"
msgstr "Les Murs"

msgctxt "help/867/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans often built long and impressive walls in newly-conquered "
"territories to help hold back the encroaching barbarian hordes. These "
"walls existed in many frontier provinces, but the most famous example "
"is Hadrian's Wall, built in 128 AD. This stone barrier, which bisects "
"England from Carlisle to Newcastle-on-Tyne, is seventy-six miles long, "
"twenty feet high, and eight feet thick. In front of the wall the Romans "
"dug a V-shaped ditch thirty feet wide at the top. Fourteen forts "
"holding a total of about a thousand soldiers were built into it at "
"regular intervals. This wall helped to keep the rampaging Picts and "
"Celts from overrunning Roman settlements to the south.  \n"
"\n"
"#868Next Page#\n"
"#865Help#/#866Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les Romains construisaient souvent des murs longs et impressionnants "
"dans les territoires nouvellement conquis pour contenir les hordes "
"barbares. Ces murs existaient sur de nombreuses frontières de Province, "
"mais le plus fameux reste le Mur d'Hadrien, construit en 128 après JC. "
"Cette barrière de pierre qui coupe l'Angleterre entre Carlisle et "
"Newcastle-on-Tyne a une longueur de 125 kilomètres, une hauteur de six "
"mètres et est épais de deux mètres cinquante. En face du mur, les "
"Romains ont creusé un fossé en forme de V de neuf mètres de profondeur. "
"Quatorze forts contenant environ mille soldats furent construits à "
"intervalles réguliers. Ce mur empêcha la submersion des colonies "
"romaines du sud par les Pictes et les Celtes déchaînés.\n"
"#868Page Suivante#\n"
"#865Aide#/#866Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/868/0"
msgid "Roman Provincial Walls (cont.)"
msgstr "Les Murs des Provinces"

msgctxt "help/868/1"
msgid ""
"A second more modest wall was built even further north in Britain by "
"Antoninus Pius, Hadrian's successor. Less is known about this "
"structure, since it was made of blocks of turf instead of stone and "
"thus has not withstood the wear of the ages the way Hadrian's wall has. "
"Antoninus Pius' wall ran across Scotland, from the Firth of Forth to "
"the Clyde. It may have been more typical of Roman provinical walls than "
"Hadrian's creation; provincial walls in general were meant to last only "
"until the province had been thoroughly pacified and its borders "
"secured.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#867Previous Page#\n"
"#865Help#/#866Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Un second mur plus modeste fut même construit plus au nord de la "
"Grande-Bretagne par Antonin le Pieux, le successeur d'Hadrien. Sa "
"structure est moins connue, comme il était fait de tourbe au lieu de "
"pierre et il n'a pas traversé les âges comme celui d'Hadrien. Le mur "
"d'Antonin le Pieux traversait l'Ecosse de l'estuaire du Forth à la "
"Clyde. Il était cependant plus typique des murs de provinces que celui "
"d'Hadrien, la vocation de ces murs étant de rester en place le temps "
"nécessaire à la pacification de la Province et à la sécurisation des "
"frontières.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#867Page Précédente#\n"
"#865Aide#/#866Trucs#"

