msgctxt "help/880/0"
msgid "Help with Forts"
msgstr "Aide : Les forts"

msgctxt "help/880/1"
msgid ""
"You may build as many as ten Cohort Forts in your Province, anywhere "
"except on mountains and atop other settlements. Each fort creates a "
"Cohort, or army, that you command. A Cohort will appear on your "
"Province Level map as an army beneath a waving battle standard, or "
"banner. The first Cohort you organize will be your Prima Cohors (First "
"Cohort), and each additional one will have its own name, makeup, and "
"ever-changing morale. The forces of your Legion (your entire armed "
"forces) will be divided evenly among the forts you build, so that the "
"more forts you have, the smaller each Cohort will be. You will manage "
"your Legion in your Forum.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#881Tips# / #882History#"
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez construire jusqu'à dix forts dans vos provinces, partout "
"sauf sur les montagnes et au sommet d'autre implantations. Chaque fort "
"crée une cohorte, ou armée, que vous commandez. La cohorte apparaît sur "
"la carte de la Province comme une armée sous un étendard de bataille, "
"ou bannière. La première cohorte s'appellera Prima Cohors et chaque "
"nouvelle aura son propre nom. Les forces de votre légion (toutes vos "
"forces armées) sont partagées équitablement entre les forts, de telle "
"sorte que plus vous avez de forts, moins la Cohorte est puissante. Vous "
"pouvez gérer vos légions dans votre Forum.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#881Trucs# / #882Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/881/0"
msgid "Tips for Forts"
msgstr "Trucs : les forts"

msgctxt "help/881/1"
msgid ""
"At the start of the game, you may find it too expensive to build a "
"sizable legion.  Building too many forts will result in a very weak "
"cohorts.\n"
"\n"
"Once you have built provincial walls, make sure you have cohorts close "
"enough to them so that armies that attack the walls can be met before "
"they breach them.  The best way of doing this is to have different "
"cohorts on different areas of the map.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#880Help# / #882History#"
msgstr ""
"Au début du jeu, vous pouvez trouver la constitution d'un grande légion "
"trop chère. Le fait de construire trop de forts affaiblit les cohortes.\n"
"\n"
"Après avoir construit des murs provinciaux, assurez-vous de la présence "
"d'une cohorte à proximité pour qu'elle puisse aller à la rencontre des "
"armées attaquant le mur avant l'ouverture d'une brèche. Le meilleur "
"moyen est d'avoirs des cohortes à plusieurs endroits de la carte.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#880Aide# / #882Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/882/0"
msgid "Roman Forts"
msgstr "Les Forts Romains"

msgctxt "help/882/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans built hundreds, if not thousands, of temporary military "
"forts called casta during their conquest of the Mediterranean. There "
"was a standard design for each fort that the soldiers had to adhere to "
"during construction: a rectangular outer wall with a grid of streets "
"and a wide central area used as a forum, with each group of soldiers "
"having its own predetermined block of barracks.  The casta functioned "
"primarily as staging areas for the Empire's armies. Since their purpose "
"was usually offensive, not defensive, they were often sited at river "
"crossings and route intersections instead of defensible hilltops. A "
"number of these forts later grew into towns of the Middle Ages. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#880Help#/#881Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Les Romains construisirent des centaines, si ce n'est des milliers de "
"forts militaires temporaires appelés Casta durant leur conquête de la "
"Méditerranée. Leur agencement était standardisé et les soldats devaient "
"en tenir compte pendant la construction: un rempart rectangulaire, un "
"quadrillage de rues et une large allée centrale servant de Forum, les "
"baraquements étant assignés d'avance à chaque groupe de soldats. Le "
"premier but du casta était d'être une étape pour les armées de "
"l'Empire. Leur vocation étant offensive et non défensive, on les "
"trouvait plus souvent au croisement de deux rivières ou de deux routes "
"qu'au sommet d'une colline. Nombre de ces forts sont ensuite devenus "
"des villes au Moyen-Age.\n"
"\n"
"#880Aide#/#881Trucs#"

