msgctxt "help/1000/0"
msgid "Help with Ports"
msgstr "Aide: les Ports"

msgctxt "help/1000/1"
msgid ""
"Ports provide trade access to lands overseas. When you build a port, it "
"may do business with the province indicated by the white arrow on its "
"side of your Province Map. A Port needs a Warehouse, but does not need "
"a Work Camp. Goods brought into the port will remain in its Warehouse "
"until it is either used by a City Level business, or sent to the "
"Emperor at his request.\n"
"Each ship you see in the ocean on your Province map carries a specific "
"cargo load. Ships come into a port, unload their cargo, and leave. You "
"may right-click on any ship to see what type of cargo it is carrying. "
"When you build a Shipyard adjacent to a Port, it increases the number "
"of ships plying your waters, and so will boost your trade. \n"
"\n"
"#1001Tips# / #1002History#"
msgstr ""
"Les ports offrent un accès commercial outremer. Lorsque vous "
"construisez un port, il commerce avec la province indiquée par la "
"flèche blanche à cet endroit de la carte. Un port nécessite un entrepôt "
"mais pas de chantier. Les marchandises amenées au port restent dans "
"l'entrepôt jusqu'à ce qu'elles soient utilisées par une industrie de la "
"Cité, ou envoyées à l'Empereur.\n"
"\n"
"Chaque bateau visible transporte une cargaison spécifique. Ils viennent "
"au port, déchargent leur cargaison et repartent. Pour connaître la "
"nature de la cargaison, cliquez sur le bouton droit. Lorsque vous "
"construisez un chantier naval près d'un port, il augmente le nombre de "
"bateaux voguant sur vos eaux et stimule votre commerce. \n"
"#1001Trucs# / #1002Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/1001/0"
msgid "Tips for Ports"
msgstr "Trucs: les Ports"

msgctxt "help/1001/1"
msgid ""
"Before you build a port, look to see where ships first hit the coast of "
"your province.  You may want to eventually build ports on either side "
"of this point, to ensure you \"catch\" all the ships that come from a sea "
"lane. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1000Help# / #1002History#"
msgstr ""
"Avant de construire un port, vérifiez l'endroit de la côte abordé en "
"priorité par les bateaux. Vous pouvez ensuite construire des ports des "
"deux côtés de ce point, pour être sur d'attraper tous les bateaux de "
"cette voie maritime. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1000Aide# / #1002Histoire#"

msgctxt "help/1002/0"
msgid "Roman Ports"
msgstr "Les ports romains"

msgctxt "help/1002/1"
msgid ""
"Since the Roman Empire surrounded and controlled the entirety of the "
"Mediterranean sea, it was natural that much of its trade should go by "
"ship. Roman ports were as well-engineered as everything else they "
"built. Each port had several wharves, divided up by type of trade.  "
"Near the wharves were the horrea, warehouses for goods. Some warehouses "
"were specialized for one type of good, but most held a diverse variety "
"of commodities. \n"
"\n"
" The city of Ostia, at the mouth of the Tiber, was Rome's port. It "
"featured more than three hundred horrea, the largest one 218 by 169 "
"yards in size. The port had to be refurbished and rebuilt several times \n"
"#1003Next Page#\n"
"#1000Help#/#1001Tips#"
msgstr ""
"l'Empire romain entourant et contrôlant la totalité de la Méditerranée, "
"il était naturel qu'une grande partie de son commerce soit maritime. "
"Les ports des romains étaient bien étudiés, comme tout ce qu'ils "
"construisaient. Chaque port possédait plusieurs quais, divisés par "
"types de commerces. Près des quais se trouvait les horrea, entrepôts de "
"marchandises. Certains entrepôts étaient spécialisés dans un type de "
"marchandise, mais la plupart comportaient une grande variété de "
"produits.\n"
"La ville d'Ostie, située à l'embouchure du Tibre, était le port de "
"Rome. Elle comportait plus de  trois cents horrea, le plus grand ayant "
"une taille de 200 mètres sur 150.Le port dût être rénové et reconstruit "
"à plusieurs reprises\n"
"#1003Page Suivante#\n"
"#1000Aide#/#1001Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/1003/0"
msgid "History of Ports (Cont..)"
msgstr "Histoire des Ports (Suite.)"

msgctxt "help/1003/1"
msgid ""
"during its history, as the Tiber brought a large amount of silt down "
"from the Appenines which tended to clog the port and render it "
"unusable. The volume of dirt carried downstream to the river's mouth is "
"so large that today Ostia, once right on the sea, is now two miles from "
"the shore.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1002Previous Page#\n"
"#1000Help#/#1001Tips#"
msgstr ""
"au cours de son histoire, le Tibre transportant une grande quantité de "
"vase depuis l'Apennin, ce qui tendait à boucher le port et à le rendre "
"inutilisable. Le volume d'alluvions transporté par le courant de "
"l'embouchure du fleuve est si grand qu'aujourd'hui Ostie, autrefois au "
"bord de l'eau, est distante de la côte de trois kilomètres.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1002Page Précédente#\n"
"#1000Aide#/#1001Trucs#"

