msgctxt "help/1109/0"
msgid "Industry in Rome"
msgstr "L'industrie à Rome"

msgctxt "help/1109/1"
msgid ""
"The city of Rome itself had little or no real industry.  Its wealth "
"sprang more from its central location in Italy (which made it a natural "
"center for trade), and from its position as the administrative capital "
"of the Empire than from any goods it could produce. The only real "
"industry in Rome centered around the necessity of providing food for "
"Rome's one million consumers. The rest of Rome's industry consisted of "
"thousands of small shopkeepers and artisans, usually operating out of "
"the first floor of some insula.  \n"
"\n"
"Rome had many specialized wholesale markets which sold only a single "
"commodity, and each had its own name. The holitorium sold vegetables, "
"the boarium \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1110Next Page#\n"
"#746Tips# / #1108List Items#"
msgstr ""
"L'industrie à Rome même était presque inexistante. Sa richesse "
"provenait plus de sa position centrale en Italie (ce qui en fit un "
"centre d'échanges naturel), et de sa position en tant que capitale "
"administrative de l'Empire, que des richesses qu'elle pouvait produire. "
"La seule vraie industrie Romaine tenait dans le souci de nourrir un "
"million de consommateurs. Le reste de l'industrie romaine se résumait "
"en milliers de petits commerces et artisans, travaillant la plupart du "
"temps au premier étage d'une Insula.\n"
"\n"
"Rome possédait de nombreux marchés spécialisés vendant un seul type de "
"bien, chacun avait son propre nom.. L'holitorium vendait des légumes, "
"le boarium\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1110Page Suivante#\n"
"#746Trucs# / #1108Afficher la liste#"

msgctxt "help/1110/0"
msgid "Industry in Rome (cont.)"
msgstr "L'industrie à Rome (suite)"

msgctxt "help/1110/1"
msgid ""
"sold cattle, the suarium sold pigs, the vinarium sold wine, and so on. "
"There were also numerous general-purpose markets, usually permanent "
"buildings covered to keep the foodstuffs from spoiling quickly in the "
"direct sunlight. These markets could become quite grand -- Trajan's "
"Market featured three tiers of shops and a great covered market hall, "
"surely a close cousin to the modern-day shopping mall. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1109Previous Page#\n"
"#746Tips# / #1108List Items#"
msgstr ""
"du bétail, le suarium des cochons, le vinarium du vin et ainsi de "
"suite. Il y avait également de nombreux marchés généralistes, édifices "
"permanents et couverts qui évitaient à l'alimentation de se désagréger "
"rapidement à la lumière du soleil. Ces marchés pouvaient devenir "
"magnifiques -- le Marché de Trajan se composait de trois niveaux de "
"boutiques et d'un grand hall de marché couvert, un proche parent des "
"centres commerciaux actuels.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1109Page Précédente#\n"
"#746Trucs# / #1108Afficher la liste#"

msgctxt "help/1111/0"
msgid "Prv Icn Industry Help4"
msgstr "Prv Icn Industry Help4"

msgctxt "help/1111/1"
msgid "There is no relevant information for this feature."
msgstr "Il n'y a aucune information sur ce sujet."

msgctxt "help/1112/0"
msgid "Order Cohort"
msgstr "Ordres aux Cohortes"

msgctxt "help/1112/1"
msgid ""
"This button allows you to select your Cohorts so that you may review "
"their status and give them orders.\n"
"\n"
"#1113Help with Cohorts#\n"
"#1114Tips for Cohorts#"
msgstr ""
"Ce bouton permet de sélectionner les Cohortes afin de réviser leur "
"statut et de leur donner des ordres.\n"
"\n"
"#1113Aide: Les Cohortes#\n"
"#1114Trucs: Les Cohortes#"

msgctxt "help/1113/0"
msgid "Help with Cohorts"
msgstr "Aide : Cohortes"

msgctxt "help/1113/1"
msgid ""
"By default, new recruits are sent equally into Cohorts, one assigned to "
"each Fort you have built on the Province Level. You may expand or "
"diminish a Cohort through the button on the Cohort info panel. The "
"\"Normal\" setting recruits an equal proportion of new troops (relative "
"to the other Cohorts), the \"Major\" setting sets a larger proportion, "
"and the \"Minor\" setting sets a smaller one. When a Cohort is set to "
"\"Demobilize,\" it will stop receiving new recruits from the training "
"pool, until you mobilize it again. \n"
"\n"
"The Order Cohort function allows you to issue orders to any of your "
"existing Cohorts.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1115Next Page#\n"
"#1114Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Par défaut, les nouvelles recrues sont équitablement réparties dans les "
"Cohortes dans les forts construits en Mode Campagne. Pour augmenter ou "
"diminuer l'effectif de l'une d'elles, utilisez le bouton Cohortes du "
"panneau Info. L'option \"Normal\" recrute une proportion égale de "
"nouvelles troupes (par rapport aux autres cohortes), l'option \"Majore\", "
"une proportion plus grande et \"Minore\" une proportion plus faible. "
"\"Démobiliser\" une Cohorte signifie la rendre inactive (et permet "
"d'incorporer ses troupes au sein d'autres Cohortes) jusqu'à une "
"remobilisation.\n"
"\n"
"La fonction Ordres aux Cohortes permet de donner des ordres à chaque "
"Cohorte existante.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1115Page Suivante#\n"
"#1114Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/1114/0"
msgid "Tips for Ordering Cohorts"
msgstr "Trucs: Ordres aux cohortes"

msgctxt "help/1114/1"
msgid ""
"Set regular patrol routes to guard walls, your city, and any areas that "
"seem to regularly fall in the path of attacking armies.\n"
"\n"
"Remember that the longer you make a patrol route, the less likely it is "
"that a cohort will be in the \"right place at the right time.\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Help#"
msgstr ""
"Envoyez régulièrement des patrouilles pour garder les murs, votre cité "
"et toutes les zones qui semblent être sur le chemin habituel des armées "
"assaillantes.\n"
"\n"
"N'oubliez pas que plus la route de la patrouille est longue, moins la "
"cohorte a de chances d'être au \"au bon endroit au bon moment\".\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Aide#"

msgctxt "help/1115/0"
msgid "Help with Cohorts (cont.)"
msgstr "Trucs: Ordre aux Cohortes (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/1115/1"
msgid ""
"You may set and assign patrol routes, send a Cohort after an enemy, or "
"to return the Cohort to its home fort. You may call upon your armies to "
"deal with several types of enemies.\n"
"\n"
"To issue orders, click on the Order Cohort button on the Province "
"Level. Your mouse pointer will change to a crosshair. Place it on the "
"Cohort you would like to command, and click.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Previous Page# \n"
"#1114Tips#"
msgstr ""
"La fonction ordres aux cohortes permet de donner des ordres à l'une de "
"vos cohortes. Vous pouvez définir et assigner la patrouille, envoyer "
"une cohorte vers l'ennemi ou la renvoyer dans son fort.\n"
"\n"
"Pour donner des ordres, cliquez sur la touche Ordre aux Cohortes au "
"Niveau Provincial. Votre curseur se transforme en épée. Placez-le sur "
"la cohorte à commander et cliquez.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Page Précédente# \n"
"#1114Trucs#"

msgctxt "help/1116/0"
msgid "Ports"
msgstr "Ports"

msgctxt "help/1116/1"
msgid ""
"Places ports to import and export goods via the sealanes to lands "
"outside your province. \n"
"\n"
"#1000Help with Ports#\n"
"#1001Tips for Ports#\n"
"#1002History of Ports#"
msgstr ""
"Placez des ports pour importer et exporter des marchandises via les "
"routes maritimes vers les terres étrangères à la province. \n"
"\n"
"#1000Aide: Les Ports#\n"
"#1001Trucs: Les Ports#\n"
"#1002Histoire des Ports#"

