msgctxt "help/1326/0"
msgid "The Flavian Emperors"
msgstr "Les Empereurs Flaviens"

msgctxt "help/1326/1"
msgid ""
"Nero's death left the soldiers of the Empire without a descendant of "
"Caesar to acclaim as Emperor. Confusion and civil war were inevitable. "
"69 AD went down in history as \"The Year of Four Emperors,\" as the "
"Imperial seat changed hands with the seasons.\n"
"\n"
"The first contenders for the position were Julius Vindex, governor of "
"Gallia Lugdunensis and commander of its armies, and Sulpicius Galba, "
"likewise governor of Hispania Tarraconensis. Vindex' neighbor, governor "
"Verginius Rufus of Upper Germany, sent his armies across the Rhine and "
"crushed Vindex, whereupon Rufus's soldiers urged him to seize the "
"Principate. But Rufus resisted and instead gave his support to Galba. "
"The Senate, eager to stop the conflict, recognized Galba as Emperor. "
"Nero's activities had drained the treasury, however, and \n"
"#1325Previous Page# / #1327 Next Page#\n"
"#3Back to Table of Contents#"
msgstr ""
"La mort de Néron laissa les soldats de l'Empire sans descendant de "
"César à acclamer comme Empereur. La confusion et la guerre civile "
"étaient inévitables. L'an 69 ap. J.-C. est connue dans l'histoire comme "
"\"l'année des quatre empereurs \"car le siège impérial changea de mains "
"avec les saisons.\n"
"Les premiers prétendants furent Julius Vindex, gouverneur de Gallia "
"Lugdunensis et commandant de ses armées, et Sulpicius Galba, alors "
"gouverneur de Hispania Tarraconensis. Le voisin de Vindex, le "
"gouverneur Verginius Rufus de la Haute Germanie, envoya ses troupes "
"traverser le Rhin et se ruer sur Vindex, où les soldats de Rufus le "
"forcèrent à saisir le Principat. Mais Rufus résista et donna son "
"soutien à Galba. Le Sénat, impatient d'arrêter le conflit, reconnut "
"Galba comme Empereur. Les activités de Néron avaient vidé le trésor et\n"
"#1325Page Précédente# / #1327 Page Suivante#\n"
"#3Retour au sommaire#"

msgctxt "help/1327/0"
msgid "The Flavian Emperors (Cont.)"
msgstr "Les Empereurs Flaviens (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/1327/1"
msgid ""
"Galba couldn't restore economic stability fast enough to suit the "
"populace; that, combined with his advanced age of 73, made him "
"unpopular. After only three months, he was assassinated by the "
"Praetorian Guard on the secret orders of Senator Marcus Salvius Otho.\n"
"\n"
"The Praetorians then acclaimed Otho as Emperor, but the provincial "
"armies of Upper and Lower Germany had other ideas, and proclaimed their "
"commander Aulus Vitellius Germanicus instead. Vitellius's army marched "
"on Rome and defeated Otho's troops. Otho committed suicide, and the "
"Senate acclaimed Vitellius -- not that they had a choice, since his "
"troops occupied the city. Out in the East, however, the other half of "
"the Roman Army had chosen still another \n"
"\n"
"#1326Previous Page# / #1328 Next Page#\n"
"#3Back to Table of Contents#"
msgstr ""
"Galba ne pouvait pas restaurer la stabilité économique assez vite pour "
"plaire à la population; cela, combiné à son grand âge de 73 ans, le "
"rendit impopulaire. Après seulement trois mois, il dut assassiné par la "
"Garde Prétorienne sur les ordres secrets du Sénateur Marcus Salvius "
"Otho.\n"
"\n"
"Les prétoriens acclamèrent alors Otho comme Empereur, mais les armées "
"provinciales de la Haute et de la Basse Germanie avaient d'autres idées "
"et proclamèrent leur commandant, Aulus Vitellius Germanicus. L'armée de "
"Vitellius se dirigea sur Rome et vainquit les troupes de Otho. Ce "
"dernier se suicida, et le Sénat acclama Vitellius -- il n'avait pas "
"d'autres choix étant donné que l'armée de celui-ci occupait la ville. A "
"l'est néanmoins, l'autre moitié de l'armée romaine avait choisi un autre\n"
"\n"
"#1326Page Précédente# / #1328 Page Suivante#\n"
"#3Retour au sommaire#"

msgctxt "help/1328/0"
msgid "The Flavian Emperors (Cont.)"
msgstr "Les Empereurs Flaviens (Suite)"

msgctxt "help/1328/1"
msgid ""
"Emperor: their commander, Titus Flavius Vespasianus, who had been "
"occupied in putting down a Jewish revolt in Judaea.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
